/* 段落记忆 · 词层 1 · 子块 c：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(1,{"sub":"c","par":{"pull":{"tw":[["draw",3],["push",1],["force",2],["tear",0],["move",6],["bring",3],["drive",2],["catch",3]],"en":"Our old car stopped in the mud after the rain. My brother had to pull the small trailer by hand. He used a rope to draw it forward while I pushed from behind with all my force. The work was slow and I began to tear my jacket on the door. A farmer came over to help, and together we managed to move the trailer to the road. He offered to bring his truck and used his tractor to drive both cars home. We did not want to catch a cold in the rain.","zh":"雨后我们那辆旧车陷在泥里。弟弟只好用手拖那个小挂车。他用绳子往前拉，我在后面使劲推。活儿很慢，我的外套在车门上开始撕开了。一位农夫过来帮忙，我俩一起把挂车挪到了路上。他提出开他的卡车来，最后用拖拉机把两辆车都拖回了家。我们可不想在雨里感上风寒。"},"sense":{"tw":[["sensible",4],["sensitive",4],["sensor",4],["sensation",4],["feel",0],["smell",0],["detect",2],["understand",2],["logic",3]],"en":"There is a strange sensation in my left hand. I can feel the heat but I cannot feel the cold, and the doctor says the sensor in the skin has stopped working. It is still very sensitive to a light touch. I cannot smell the coffee any more either. The machine can detect the change, but nobody can understand it yet, and there is no logic in it. The doctors say the sense will come back slowly. A sensible person would rest at home, but I have work to do and my hands are the only tools I own.","zh":"我左手有一种奇怪的感觉。我能感觉到热，却感觉不到冷，医生说皮肤里的传感器已经不工作了。但它对轻微的触碰仍然很敏感。我也闻不到咖啡味了。仪器能检测到这个变化，却没人能解释，其中毫无逻辑可言。医生说这种感觉会慢慢恢复。明智的人会在家休息，可我还有活要干，而这双手是我唯一的工具。"},"picture":{"tw":[["depict",4],["pictorial",4],["photograph",0],["image",2],["illustrate",3],["figure",0],["film",0],["screen",6]],"en":"The picture on my wall is a photograph of the old harbour. It does not depict the whole town, only a small image of the boats. The book next to it is pictorial: every page has a drawing to illustrate one word. I like the figure of the boy in the corner best. In the film they showed last week, the same picture filled the whole screen for a few seconds. I bought it for almost nothing on a wet morning, and I have never wanted to sell it. It hangs a little crooked, and I have never fixed that either.","zh":"我墙上那幅画是一张旧港的照片。它没有描绘整个镇子，只有小船的一个小影像。旁边那本书是图解式的：每一页都有一幅画来解释一个词。我最喜欢角落里那个男孩的形象。在他们上周放的那部电影里，同一幅画面有几秒钟铺满了整个银幕。我是在一个雨天早晨几乎白捡来的，也从来没想卖掉它。它挂得有点歪，我也一直没去扶正。"},"nose":{"tw":[["nosy",4],["nasal",4],["snout",3],["scent",0],["poke",0],["push",2],["throat",6],["front",2]],"en":"The dog has a cold nose and a very nasal bark. Its snout is always in the long grass, following some scent. Do not poke it and do not push it away; it will only come back. The hair on its throat is white, and the front of its face is black. My nosy neighbour says the dog knows everything that happens in this street. During the heat of the day it sleeps under the table and does not move at all. At night it pushes the gate open with its snout and walks the whole street alone.","zh":"那只狗鼻子凉凉的，叫声带着很重的鼻音。它的口鼻总埋在深草里，追着某种气味。别去戳它，也别把它推开，它只会再回来。它喉咙上的毛是白的，脸的前部是黑的。我那位爱打听的邻居说，这条街上发生的事这只狗全知道。白天最热的时候它就趴在桌子底下睡，一动也不动。到了夜里它用口鼻把大门顶开，独自把整条街走一遍。"},"office":{"tw":[["official",4],["officiate",4],["position",0],["post",0],["headquarters",3],["duty",2],["staff",2],["department",6]],"en":"The office is on the third floor of an old building. The official letter says my position starts on Monday. Our headquarters is in another city, and this post is only a small department of four people. The staff are kind. My first duty is to answer the phone; I also have to officiate at the morning meeting. The lift has not worked since March, so we all take the stairs, and the stairs are the only place where anybody speaks freely. The staff say the department will move next year, and nobody is sorry about it.","zh":"办公室在一栋旧楼的三层。公函上说我的职位周一开始。我们的总部在另一个城市，这个岗位只是一个四人的小部门。同事们都很和气。我的第一项职责是接电话，还得主持晨会。电梯从三月起就坏了，所以我们全都走楼梯，而楼梯是唯一能让人畅所欲言的地方。同事们说这个部门明年要搬走，没人为此难过。"},"please":{"tw":[["pleasant",4],["pleasure",4],["delight",0],["satisfy",2],["enchant",3],["wish",2],["displease",1],["ask",6]],"en":"It is hard to please my aunt. A pleasant word in the morning will delight her, but nothing can satisfy her for long. The garden does not enchant her any more. I only wish she would ask for what she wants; then I could please her at once. Last week I displeased her by arriving late. It is no pleasure to sit in that room with her. She says the house is too quiet, and I think that is the whole trouble. I ask her again what would please her, and she only says the name of my mother.","zh":"要让我姑妈满意很难。早上一句好听的话能让她高兴，但什么都不能让她满意太久。花园已经不再让她着迷了。我只希望她能把想要的东西说出来，那样我马上就能让她高兴。上周我迟到惹她不快。和她坐在那个房间里毫无乐趣可言。她说屋子太安静了，我想这就是全部的问题所在。我又问她什么能让她开心，她只说出了我母亲的名字。"},"mind":{"tw":[["mental",4],["head",0],["tend",3],["forget",1],["manage",2],["worry",3],["notice",2],["idea",0],["listen",0]],"en":"There is too much in my mind this week. My head is full of small numbers, and I tend to forget names. The doctor says it is not a mental problem, only tiredness. I try to manage one thing at a time. Do not worry, she says, and notice what you eat. It is a good idea, and I should listen to her, but I never do. My mother had the same mind and the same habit of not listening to anybody. This morning I put the keys in the fridge and the milk in my bag.","zh":"这星期我脑子里装的东西太多了。我满脑子都是小数字，还容易忘名字。医生说这不是精神上的问题，只是累。我试着一次只处理一件事。别担心，她说，注意你吃的东西。这是个好主意，我该听她的，可我从来不听。我母亲也有同样的脑子，也有同样的、谁的话都不听的习惯。今天早上我把钥匙放进冰箱，把牛奶塞进了包里。"},"notice":{"tw":[["notify",4],["bill",0],["knock",3],["sign",2],["ignore",1],["check",6],["card",0],["discover",0],["mention",3]],"en":"Did you notice the notice on the door? A small card says we must notify the office if we leave. Nobody told me about it; they did not even knock. There is a sign above the bell, but people ignore it every single day. I had to check the bill three times before I discovered the extra line at the bottom. When I asked about it, the man at the desk did not mention it once. He only looked at his hands. The next day a card was on the door again, with the same three lines on it.","zh":"你注意到门上那张告示了吗？一张小卡片说我们离开时必须通知办公室。没人跟我说过这件事，他们连门都没敲。铃上方有个标牌，可人们每天都视而不见。我把账单核对了三遍，才发现底部多出的那一行。我去问时，柜台后面那个人一次也没提。他只是看着自己的手。第二天门上又出现了一张卡片，还是那三行字。"},"pass":{"tw":[["passage",4],["clear",3],["break",3],["change",2],["fail",1],["carry",3],["leave",2],["draw",0]],"en":"You cannot pass this road in winter. The passage over the hill is clear for only three months, and one bad storm can break it completely. If the weather does not change, we will fail to reach the village at all. Two men carry the mail on foot and leave before dawn. I draw a map every year and it is never the same twice. Still, the post always gets through in the end, and that is the only thing that matters up here. One year the passage was clear in February, and everybody talked about it until June.","zh":"冬天你没法通过这条路。翻过山口那条通道只有三个月是通的，一场坏风暴就能把它彻底毁掉。如果天气不变，我们根本到不了那个村子。两个人徒步送信，天不亮就出发。我每年画一张地图，从来没重过样。可邮件最后总能送到，而在这山里那是唯一要紧的事。有一年二月山口就通了，大家一直议论到六月。"},"present":{"tw":[["presence",4],["face",0],["date",3],["inform",2],["past",1],["stage",0],["state",2],["deliver",0]],"en":"At present there is no water in the tank. The presence of two engineers did not help; they only informed us of the date of the repair and left. On the stage above the door someone has written the state of the pump every day for ten years. In the past we never had to check it. The man who comes to deliver the parts knows the problem by heart, but he did not show his face for three days. Until then we carry water from the well in the yard, which is what everyone did in the past.","zh":"目前水箱里没有水。两位工程师在场也没用；他们只是通知了我们维修的日期就走了。门上方那块平台上，有人十年来每天都记下水泵的状态。从前我们根本不用检查。来送零件的那个人对这个问题了如指掌，可他整整三天没露面。在那之前，我们从院子里的井里打水，过去大家也都是这么做的。"},"mouth":{"tw":[["oral",4],["lip",0],["shout",3],["tongue",6],["speak",0],["sing",3],["communicate",2],["talk",0]],"en":"Keep your mouth closed when you chew. The oral exam next week will test how you open a speech, and my teacher wants us to speak slowly. When you shout, the tongue moves differently than when you sing. She says a mouth can talk all day and communicate nothing at all. Her lower lip is dry and her voice is thin now. Do not touch the microphone with your lips. My mother puts a finger to her lips whenever I open mine at the table. She never learned to sing, she says, because nobody in the house ever listened.","zh":"嚼东西的时候把嘴闭上。下周的口试要考你怎么开头演讲，老师要我们说慢一点。喊的时候，舌头的动作和唱歌时不一样。她说一张嘴能说一整天却什么也没表达。她的下唇很干，嗓音如今也细弱了。别用嘴唇碰麦克风。她说她从没学会唱歌，因为家里从来没人听。"},"move":{"tw":[["motion",4],["act",2],["beat",3],["cause",2],["continue",6],["run",0],["begin",3],["change",2]],"en":"We have to move the piano before Friday. The motion of the truck on these roads will damage it, so we wrap every leg in cloth. I cannot act alone; two people have to lift at the same time, to the same beat. Nothing will cause more trouble than the stairs. If it starts to rain we will begin again in the morning. Water can change the shape of wood in one night, so we cannot stay outside. The whole move should take two hours if nobody runs. We will continue with the small boxes indoors.","zh":"我们得在周五前把钢琴搬走。卡车在这些路上的颠簸会把它弄坏，所以我们把每条腿都裹上布。我一个人做不了；两个人得同时抬，按同一个节拍。没有比那几级楼梯更麻烦的了。要是下起雨来，我们就第二天早上重来。水一夜之间就能改变木头的形状，所以不能放在外面。只要没人乱跑，整个搬运两小时就能完。"},"name":{"tw":[["nominal",4],["call",0],["refer",6],["discover",0],["raise",3],["appoint",2],["family",2],["figure",0]],"en":"Nobody knows the real name of the old man at the gate. People call him 'the captain', but that is only a nominal title; nobody has been able to discover where it came from. His family name is carved above the door, and I have to refer to it every morning when I raise the flag. The committee will appoint a new watchman in June. The figure of a woman on the gate carries the same name. Even the map of the town carries the same name in its corner. It has been there since 1893, and nobody has ever tried to change it.","zh":"没人知道大门口那位老人的真名。大家叫他「船长」，可那只是个名义上的称呼；没人能查清它的来历。他的姓氏刻在门楣上，我每天早上升旗时都得提到它。委员会六月要任命一名新看守。大门上那个女人的雕像也带着同一个名字。"},"need":{"tw":[["needy",4],["ask",0],["want",0],["demand",0],["cost",3],["condition",2],["poverty",2],["cry",3]],"en":"Tell me what you need. Do not ask twice and do not demand; just say it once. The cost of the repairs is small, but the condition of the roof is not, and sooner or later we will have to deal with it. There are two needy families in this street, and one of them lives in real poverty. I heard a child cry last night, in the house at the corner. I am sure they want nothing more than a warm room. The cost of coal has gone up again, and the condition of those houses is a demand nobody will answer.","zh":"告诉我你需要什么。别问两遍，也别强求，说一次就够了。修理的花费不大，可屋顶的状况不好，迟早得处理。这条街上有两户穷苦人家，其中一户真的是一贫如洗。昨晚我听见一个孩子在哭，就在拐角那栋房子里。我敢肯定，他们想要的不过是一间暖和的屋子。煤价又涨了，而那些房子的状况是没人愿意回应的一项诉求。"},"note":{"tw":[["annotate",4],["bill",0],["quote",6],["line",0],["mark",0],["read",6],["state",2],["excuse",3]],"en":"I left a note on the table. It says the bill has been paid and the spare key is under the pot. I had to annotate the last page, because the small line at the bottom is easy to miss. Do not quote me on any of this, and do not read the note to the king; he will only look for an excuse. The state of the accounts is written in the same note, and I put a mark next to every name. If you read it again in the morning, do not quote the last line to anybody.","zh":"我在桌上留了张字条。上面写着账单已经付了，备用钥匙在花盆底下。最后一页我不得不加注，因为底下那一小行很容易看漏。这些话别引我的话，也别把字条念给国王听，他只会找个借口。账目状况也写在同一张字条上，我在每个名字旁都做了记号。如果你早上再读一遍，别把最后一行引给任何人听。"},"nurse":{"tw":[["nursery",4],["hold",0],["midwife",3],["care",2],["entertain",0],["matron",3],["feed",2],["nanny",0]],"en":"The nurse comes at six and the matron at eight. In the nursery next door there are twelve small beds, and a nanny feeds the smallest ones by hand. The midwife who delivered my brother still works here; she says care is the only medicine that never runs out. I hold the lamp for her while she works. She will entertain the children for an hour and then send them all to bed. In the winter she stays until midnight, and nobody asks her to. The children call her by her first name, which the matron does not like at all.","zh":"护士六点来，护士长八点来。隔壁的育婴室里摆着十二张小床，一位保姆用手一口口喂最小的那几个。当年接生我弟弟的助产士如今还在这儿干；她说照护是唯一永远不会用完的药。她干活时我替她举着灯。她会陪孩子们玩一个小时，然后把他们全都打发上床。"},"position":{"tw":[["posit",4],["lay",0],["dress",3],["move",2],["office",0],["face",3],["state",2],["post",0]],"en":"My position in the office is a small one. I lay out the letters in the morning and move the files from one post to another. The face of the building is being repaired, so we dress the windows with paper. I would posit that nobody here knows what the final state of the plan will be. However, we will keep working. The sign on the door still carries the old name. Every day I do the same three things, and every day they take the same time. My desk is by the window, and I can see the river from it.","zh":"我在办公室里的职位很小。早上我把信件摊开，把文件从一个岗位挪到另一个岗位。大楼的正面正在维修，所以我们用纸把窗户糊起来。我敢假定这里没人知道这个计划最终的状态是什么。不管怎样，我们还会继续干。门上的牌子还挂着旧名字。"},"post":{"tw":[["poster",4],["carry",0],["express",3],["call",2],["press",6],["office",0],["locate",3],["list",2],["position",0]],"en":"Every post brings two letters and a newspaper. The office cannot locate the missing parcel, and nobody can tell me which list it is on. I put a poster on the wall: 'Do not post cash'. We carry the bags to the express box before nine, and the press calls us every afternoon, sometimes twice. My position here is simple: I sort the mail and I keep quiet. At Christmas the bags are so heavy that two of us have to carry them. Nobody writes letters any more, they say, but the bags are never lighter.","zh":"每一班邮件送来两封信和一份报纸。办公室查不到那个丢失的包裹，也没人告诉我它在哪张清单上。我在墙上贴了张海报：「勿寄现金」。九点前我们把邮袋送到快递箱，报社每天下午都打电话来，有时打两次。我在这里的岗位很简单：分拣邮件，闭嘴干活。"},"race":{"tw":[["run",0],["heat",3],["act",2],["contest",6],["wash",0],["tear",3],["move",2],["rush",0]],"en":"The race begins at noon. Nobody can act as if it is only a game: the heat of the day will decide half of it. We watch from the bank, where the water can wash the mud off our shoes. A hundred people run, and the crowd cannot move at all when the rush starts at the first corner. This contest is older than the town. One year the wind was strong enough to tear every flag off the poles. Another year the river rose and the whole contest was moved to the road above the town.","zh":"比赛中午开始。谁也不能装作这只是一场游戏：当天的暑气会决定一半的胜负。我们在河岸上看，那里的水能洗掉鞋上的泥。一百个人在跑，第一个弯道拥挤开始时，人群根本动不了。这项比赛比镇子还老。有一年风大得把所有旗子都从杆子上扯了下来。又有一年河水涨了，整场比赛挪到了镇子上面那条路上。"},"number":{"tw":[["numeric",4],["square",3],["company",2],["total",3],["count",0],["several",6],["least",6],["bit",0]],"en":"Write your number at the top of the page. The system is numeric: no letters, no dashes. Our company counts every call, and the total last month was a little over nine hundred. Several of them were wrong. A square of paper with the same number is pinned to the board. I am tired, and it takes the least bit of noise to make me lose the count. The office has a number for everything: the door, the phone, the pile of paper on the shelf. I write mine on the back of my hand so that I will not forget it.","zh":"把号码写在页面顶端。格式是纯数字：不要字母，不要短横。我们公司统计每一通电话，上个月的总数略超九百。其中有几通是错的。一张写着同样号码的方纸钉在告示板上。我累了，一点点响声就能让我数乱。"},"school":{"tw":[["scholastic",4],["educate",2],["conservatory",3],["college",6],["train",0],["swim",2],["graduate",6],["civilise",0]],"en":"The school stands at the end of the street. Its scholastic record is not famous, but it has educated half the village. There is a conservatory behind it where the children train in music, and a small pool where they swim in summer. My sister went on to college and will graduate in July. Nobody here speaks of civilising anybody; they only want the children to be able to read. The building is old, and the roof was repaired with money the parents collected themselves. Every year the oldest children repaint the front wall before the summer.","zh":"学校坐落在街的尽头。它的学业成绩并不出名，却教出了半个村子的人。后面有个玻璃琴房，孩子们在那里练音乐；还有个小水池，夏天他们在里面游泳。我妹妹后来上了大学，七月就要毕业。这里没人说什么开化谁，他们只想让孩子能读书。"},"man":{"tw":[["human",0],["black",3],["island",2],["woman",1],["boy",6],["piece",0],["white",3],["work",2],["old",6],["world",3]],"en":"The old man lived alone on the island for eleven years after his wife died. He was the only human being there, and for a long time he did not see a woman or a boy. His house was one long piece of white stone above the black rocks, and he kept it in good work by mending the roof every spring. When people asked how he could bear it, he said the world was large enough for one man if he watched it closely. Now he is gone, and only the garden shows where he lived.","zh":"妻子去世后，那个老人在岛上独自住了十一年。整座岛上只有他一个人，很长一段时间里，他见不到一个女人，也见不到一个男孩。他的房子是黑礁石上头一块长长的白石头，每年春天他修一次屋顶，把它收拾得挺像样。有人问他怎么熬得住，他说，一个人只要看得够仔细，这世界对他就够大了。现在他不在了，只有那片园子还显示他曾经住过。"},"manage":{"tw":[["care",0],["build",3],["act",2],["fail",1],["help",6],["deal",0],["meet",3],["control",2],["need",6],["handle",0]],"en":"She has to manage a small shop and a family at the same time, and she does it well. She will build the week's plan on Sunday, deal with the suppliers on Monday, and meet her customers every day. If she should fail at anything, she does not need anyone to tell her. She can handle a difficult customer better than most people I know, and she is never rude. The one thing she cannot control is her own tiredness. I act as if I were fine, she says, and then I take care of myself on Sunday. Her sister comes in to help on Saturdays.","zh":"她既要管一家小店，又要管家，两头都顾得很好。她星期天把一周的打算排出来，星期一跟供货的人打交道，每天还要见客人。要是哪件事没办成，她不用别人说。难缠的客人，她应付得比我认识的多数人都好，而且从不失礼。唯一她管不住的就是自己的累。她说：我就装作没事，然后星期天再照顾自己。星期六她妹妹会过来搭把手。"},"miss":{"tw":[["drop",0],["cut",3],["woman",2],["hit",1],["play",6],["lose",0],["forget",3],["avoid",2],["title",6],["escape",0]],"en":"The woman in the next seat told me not to miss the first ten minutes of the play. She had a title in her hand and kept checking it. If you drop in late, she said, you lose the whole point. I did not want to hit anyone with my bag, so I cut along the wall and sat down quickly. I tried to avoid the man with the loud voice, but I could not forget how close I had come to being late. That day I learned to leave the house early and never miss a train again. There is no escape from that lesson once it is learned.","zh":"邻座那位女士叫我千万别错过这出戏开头那十分钟。她手里捏着节目单，一遍遍看。她说：你要是迟到了再进去，整出戏的意思就丢了。我不想用包撞到人，就贴着墙边挤过去，赶紧坐下。我想躲开那个嗓门大的男人，可忘不掉自己差一点就迟到。那天我算是学乖了：出门要早，再也不能误车。这教训一旦学到手，就再也躲不开了。"},"open":{"tw":[["clear",0],["establish",3],["move",2],["close",1],["next",6],["subject",0],["gap",3],["start",2],["round",6],["loose",0]],"en":"The committee met in an open room on the second floor, with a clear view of the yard. Before the start of business they had to establish who would speak first, then move the tables into a loose round so everyone could see the others. There was a gap at the door, which they left open for air. Half the subject that day was the next budget, but by six o'clock they had still not voted to close the meeting. In the end they agreed to carry the matter over to the following week, and the room emptied in a minute.","zh":"委员会在二楼一间敞亮的屋子里开会，从那儿能把院子看得清清楚楚。开会之前，他们得先定下谁第一个发言，然后把桌子摆成一个松松的圈，好让每个人都看得见别人。门那儿有条缝，他们就让它敞着透气。那天的议题有一半是下一年的预算，可到六点他们还没表决要不要散会。最后他们说好把这事推到下个星期，屋子里一分钟就走空了。"},"question":{"tw":[["doubt",0],["problem",3],["ask",2],["answer",1],["whether",6],["head",0],["pump",3],["subject",2],["reason",6],["wonder",3]],"en":"The teacher would ask one question and then wait, with her head a little to one side. There was no doubt in her mind that a good problem is worth more than a quick answer. I wonder, she would say, whether any of you can tell me the reason for this. Then she would pump the water out of an old pipe to show us what she meant. The subject of the lesson was pressure, but what she really taught us was to sit with a question instead of reaching for the first thing that came.","zh":"老师会先提一个问题，然后等着，头微微偏到一边。她心里从不怀疑：一个好问题比一个快答案值钱。她会说：我倒想知道，你们谁说得清这里头的道理。接着她会用一根旧管子把水抽出来，让我们看看她是什么意思。那节课的主题是压力，可她真正教我们的是：守着一个问题待着，别急着去抓头一个冒出来的东西。"},"quiet":{"tw":[["calm",5],["compose",3],["comfort",2],["active",1],["little",6],["silence",0],["lull",3],["order",2],["usual",6],["smooth",0]],"en":"After the storm the sea went quiet, and a smooth calm spread over the water. My father, who is not usually a still man, sat on the wall and said nothing. It is a lull, he told me, not a silence. The little harbour was in good order again, and the boats lay at rest in it. He is active all day and does not know how to compose himself, but on that evening he found comfort in just sitting. I did not disturb him; I only watched the light move.","zh":"暴风雨过后，海静了下来，一片平顺的安宁铺在水面上。我爸平时不是个能静住的人，那天却坐在墙上什么也不说。他告诉我：这只是暂时的平息，不是真正的寂静。小港湾又整整齐齐了，船都安安静静停在里头。他一天到晚闲不住，不知道该怎么让自己沉下来，可那天晚上，光是坐着就让他觉得宽慰。我没去打扰他，只是看着光线一点点移动。"},"raise":{"tw":[["climb",0],["carry",3],["bet",2],["lower",1],["pay",6],["farm",0],["draw",3],["better",2],["benefit",6],["fire",0]],"en":"The men on the farm had to raise the new barn before the winter. They would climb the frame with a rope, carry each beam up by hand, and draw it into place. One of them made a bet that he could lift the heaviest piece alone, and lost. The owner agreed to pay them better for the extra days, because the benefit to the whole village was clear. In the evening they lit a fire by the road and talked about the year to come. Nobody mentioned the lower price of grain.","zh":"农场上的那些人得赶在入冬前把新谷仓立起来。他们拿绳子爬上架子，把每根梁用手抬上去，再拉到位。有一个人打赌说他一个人能抬起最重的那根，结果输了。东家答应对多加的这几天给更好的工钱，因为这对整个村子都有好处，谁都看得见。傍晚他们在路边生了一堆火，聊起明年。没人提粮价走低的事。"},"record":{"tw":[["book",3],["card",3],["list",2],["erase",1],["consecutive",6],["enter",0],["cut",3],["save",2],["straight",6],["read",0]],"en":"The clerk kept a record of every visitor in a thick book by the door. She would enter the name, read the card, and then write a straight list of the hours each one stayed. No two entries were consecutive; the numbers jumped about all day. If she made a mistake she would erase it with a small knife and cut the page away. I save these, she said, because one day someone will want to know who came and went. She has kept the same record for thirty years.","zh":"门房在门边一本厚本子里记下每个来访的人。她会写下名字，看一眼证件，然后把每人待了几个钟头一行行直着列出来。没有两条是挨着的，一整天数字都在乱跳。要是写错了，她就用小刀刮掉，把那一块裁下来。她说：这些我都留着，总有一天有人想知道谁来过、谁走了。同一本记录她记了三十年。"},"remember":{"tw":[["think",0],["mind",3],["mention",2],["forget",1],["maybe",6],["recall",0],["qualify",3],["associate",2],["imagine",6],["retrieve",0]],"en":"I cannot always remember names, but I can recall a face for years. My mother would mention someone at dinner and I would think, without being able to qualify it, that I had met them before. Maybe that is why I associate certain rooms with certain people. I try to imagine what my grandfather looked like, and I can still retrieve the sound of his voice. What I forget is small: the day, the street, the colour of the door. He said once that the mind keeps what matters and lets the rest go.","zh":"我不总能记住名字，但一张脸我能记好些年。饭桌上我妈提到某人，我心里就会觉得以前见过，可说不清是怎么个见过法。也许正因如此，我总把某些屋子和某些人连在一块儿。我试着去想我爷爷长什么样，还能把他说话的声调捞回来。我忘掉的都是些小事：哪一天、哪条街、门是什么颜色。他生前说过，脑子留下来的都是要紧的，其余的全放走了。"},"ride":{"tw":[["drive",0],["boat",3],["climb",2],["walk",1],["bike",6],["sit",0],["bus",3],["continue",2],["track",6],["mount",0]],"en":"We used to ride the old bus up the valley every summer. My father would drive to the station, leave the car, and climb aboard with two bags. On the boat we would sit at the back and watch the track of white water behind us. Sometimes he would let me mount his bike and walk it along the road beside him. When the light began to go he would say we should continue a little further, and we always did. I have never found a journey I liked better.","zh":"每年夏天我们都坐那趟老旧的公共汽车上山谷去。我爸先开车到车站，把汽车留下，再拎着两个包爬上车。在船上我们就坐在船尾，看身后那道白色的水痕。有时候他让我骑上他的自行车，他在旁边推着走。天光开始暗下来时，他总说再往前一点吧，而我们每回都真的往前了。我后来再没遇到过比那更让我喜欢的旅程。"},"right":{"tw":[["good",0],["floor",3],["change",2],["left",1],["without",6],["proper",5],["access",3],["hand",2],["back",6],["correct",0]],"en":"The right to walk on that ground belonged to the village, but nobody had the proper papers. A man came from the city and put a fence across the path, so we had to go round by the left side of the hill. My grandfather said it was not good, and that without access to the water the farms would change hands within a year. He wrote to the council and got the correct answer at last: the fence came down. He kept the letter in his hand all the way home, and on the back he wrote the date. Then he laid it on the floor of the hall and read it to us twice.","zh":"在那片地上行走的权利本来是村里的，可谁手里都没有正式的文件。城里来了个人，在路当中拉起一道栅栏，我们只好绕到山左边走。我爷爷说这样不行，要是取不到水，这些农地一年之内就得易主。他给镇公所写了信，最后得了个正确的答复：栅栏拆了。他一路把那封信捏在手里回家，还在背面写下了日期。"},"rise":{"tw":[["climb",3],["head",3],["change",2],["fall",1],["decline",6],["grow",2],["wave",3],["look",2],["surge",6],["jump",3]],"en":"We climbed to the head of the valley to watch the sun rise. The price of grain had begun to decline that spring, and the farmers said the change would not last. They would look at the sky and guess, and when the wind came the wheat would wave like water. In a dry year the crop can grow quickly and then fall in a single night. My uncle said the worst thing was the surge of hope in June. Then he jumped the wall and went in for breakfast.","zh":"我们爬到山谷顶上去看日出。那年春天粮价开始往下走，种地的人说这变化长不了。他们会抬头看天、凭经验猜，风一来，麦子就像水一样起伏。碰上旱年，庄稼能长得飞快，然后一夜之间全倒。我叔说最难受的是六月里那阵子希望往上涌的时候。说完他跳过墙，进屋吃早饭去了。"},"round":{"tw":[["around",0],["bottom",3],["call",2],["square",1],["final",6],["beat",0],["rubbish",3],["change",2],["match",6],["attack",0]],"en":"The final round of the match was played in front of a small crowd. There is a square of grass at the bottom of our street, and the players had to walk around a rubbish bin to reach it. The drummer would beat his drum and call out the score after every point. Our side came under attack early, and the coach had to change the plan twice. It was a hard game, and by the end the whole team was too tired to speak. They lost, but the crowd stood up for them all the same.","zh":"比赛的最后一轮是在一小群观众面前踢的。我们这条街尽头有块方方的草地，球员得绕过一只垃圾桶才能走到场上。鼓手每得一分就敲鼓、报比分。我们这边一开场就被压着打，教练不得不两次改打法。那是场硬仗，到终场时整队人都累得说不出话。他们输了，可观众还是都站起来为他们鼓掌。"},"run":{"tw":[["carry",0],["cut",3],["break",2],["idle",1],["start",6],["course",0],["double",3],["change",2],["home",6],["draw",3]],"en":"My brother used to run the two miles home from school every day. He would cut across the field, break through the hedge, and arrive at the door with his shirt out. He never sat idle; if the weather was bad he would run the course indoors, up and down the stairs. He would draw a mark on the door frame after every run, and twice he ran a double distance on purpose, just to see what his body would do. Our mother would carry a glass of water out to him, and he would drink it standing up. That was the start of a habit that has never changed.","zh":"我哥哥从前每天从学校跑两英里回家。他抄过那片田，钻过树篱，到门口时衬衫都跑出来了。他从不闲坐着；天气不好就在屋里跑那条路线，楼上楼下地跑。每跑完一趟他就在门框上画一道记，还有两回他故意跑双倍的路，就想看看自己身体能扛成什么样。我妈会端杯水出去给他，他就站着喝。这个习惯从那时候起就没变过。"},"second":{"tw":[["back",0],["climax",3],["position",2],["first",1],["final",6],["bit",0],["pinpoint",3],["support",2],["straight",6],["minute",0]],"en":"She finished a very close second in the final race of the season. For a bit she stood at the back of the field and could not look at anyone. The climax had come in the first hundred metres, when she was still in a good position; after that the winner moved away and she could not pinpoint where she had lost the time. One minute, her coach said, and you would have had it. He asked her to hold her back straight and to support her weight on the other foot. She simply nodded.","zh":"赛季最后一场比赛，她以极小的差距拿了第二。有一小会儿，她站在场地最后头，谁也不敢看。最要紧的那一刻出现在头一百米，那时候她的位置还很好；之后领先的人跑远了，而她说不出自己是在哪儿丢掉了时间。她教练说：就差一分钟，你就拿下了。他让她把背挺直，把重心换到另一只脚上撑住。她只是点了点头。"},"sell":{"tw":[["deal",3],["clear",3],["exchange",2],["buy",1],["purchase",6],["trade",0],["market",3],["sale",2],["cash",6],["betray",0]],"en":"My father used to sell vegetables at the market on Saturday mornings. He would make one deal with the man on his left and a better one with the woman on his right, and by nine the best of the boxes were gone. He took cash and would not exchange a purchase without a receipt. Once you sell, he said, you must not betray the buyer by sending him a poor crate. He was in the trade for thirty years and never made a sale he could not stand behind. I remember him clearing the stall in the rain.","zh":"我爸从前星期六早上在集市上卖菜。他会跟左边那人讲一笔，再跟右边的女人讲一笔更好的，到九点最好的几箱就都出手了。他只收现钱，没有收据就不肯换货。他说：东西一旦卖出去，你就不能给买家发一箱烂的，那叫背叛人。他在这行做了三十年，没有一笔买卖是他不肯担的。我记得他在雨里收摊的样子。"},"set":{"tw":[["arrange",2],["bed",3],["change",2],["rise",1],["next",6],["dress",0],["charge",3],["choose",2],["break",6],["fit",0]],"en":"Every evening my grandmother would set the table before the sun began to rise. She would arrange the plates in a row, choose the bread, and then dress the salad with oil. When the heat came on she had to charge the old cooker and wait for it to fit the temperature she wanted. The next thing was the bed, which she made with a stiff cover. Nothing would make her change the order: set the table first, break the bread last. It was the same in every house she ever lived in.","zh":"每天傍晚，太阳还没下去，我奶奶就把桌子摆好了。她把盘子排成一行，挑好面包，再给沙拉浇上油。暖气一上来，她就得给那台老灶添料，等着它到她要的温度。接下来是床，她用的是硬挺的床罩。什么也改不了她那套顺序：先摆桌，最后才掰面包。她住过的每一间屋子都是这样。"},"mother":{"tw":[["maternal",4],["father",1],["care",2],["daughter",6],["generate",0],["parent",2],["husband",6],["fuss",0]],"en":"My mother was the quiet one in our house; my father made all the noise. She had a maternal way with every child on the street, and she would care for them as if they were her own. When my sister had a daughter of her own, my mother went to stay for a month and would not let anyone else take over. She and my father had been husband and wife for forty years, and she still made a fuss over his birthday. She used to say that a parent is not a person who generates rules but one who keeps them company.","zh":"在我们家，我妈是安静的那个，闹出动静的全是我爸。她对街上每个孩子都有股母性，会像对自己孩子一样照顾他们。我姐姐生下自己的女儿以后，我妈过去住了一个月，不让别人插手。她和我爸做了四十年夫妻，她还照样为他的生日忙前忙后。她生前常说，当父母不是定规矩的人，而是陪着他们的人。"},"person":{"tw":[["personify",4],["individual",0],["creature",3],["man",6],["soul",0],["tyrant",3],["woman",6],["mortal",0]],"en":"He was the kind of person who remembers your name after one meeting. My grandfather used to personify patience for me: he would let a man talk for an hour and never once look at the clock. He said that no individual is only one thing, and that the worst creature in the village had a soul as well. He had lived under a tyrant in his youth, and it had taught him to be gentle with every woman and man he met. He was, for all his faults, the most mortal and the most decent of us.","zh":"他见过一面就能记住你的名字，就是这种人。在我眼里，我爷爷简直就是耐心的化身：他能让人讲上一个钟头，一眼都不看钟。他说，没有哪一个人只是一样东西，村里最坏的家伙也有一颗心。他年轻时在暴君底下活过，这让他对遇见的每个女人男人都和和气气。他毛病不少，可他是我们当中最像个凡人、也最厚道的一个。"},"make":{"tw":[["build",0],["add",3],["act",2],["break",1],["need",6],["cause",0],["bring",3],["enough",6],["clear",0]],"en":"The old man had to make a new gate for the yard, and he would not let anyone help. He had to build it from boards he had kept for years, and add a bar across the top. It was clear from the start that he had no need of advice. He would act slowly, measure twice, and never break a piece. He said a bad joint is the cause of half the trouble in this world. He had enough wood in the end, and he did not have to bring anything from the shop. It took him nine days. The gate is still there.","zh":"老人得给院子做一扇新门，他不让别人搭手。他得用存了多年的木板来做，再在上面加一道横杠。从一开始就看得出，他不需要谁出主意。他动手很慢，量两遍，从不弄断一块料。他说这世上有一半的麻烦，都是一个接得不好的榫头造成的。最后木料够了，他也不用去铺子里拿什么。这只门他做了九天。门现在还在。"},"master":{"tw":[["control",2],["command",3],["beat",2],["tutor",6],["lord",0],["subjugate",3],["key",2],["bachelor",6],["main",0]],"en":"The old master of the little college had a bachelor's degree from a school nobody had heard of, and he never let anyone forget it. He could not control his temper when a tutor asked a question he thought foolish, and he would command silence with one hand. In his own room he was a lord. He would beat every student at chess and then explain, for an hour, why. The main reason people stayed was his library; the key to it hung at his belt. He never managed to subjugate anyone who laughed. I think that was his only weakness.","zh":"那所小学堂的老先生有个谁也没听说过的学校的学士学位，他从不让人忘记这件事。辅导老师问了个他觉得蠢的问题，他就管不住脾气，一抬手就能叫全场安静。在他自己那间屋里，他就是个老爷。下棋他谁都能赢，赢完还要讲上一个钟头为什么。人们留下来的主要原因是他的藏书室，钥匙就挂在他腰上。谁要是一笑，他就降不住谁了。我想这是他唯一的软处。"},"matter":{"tw":[["count",0],["least",3],["concern",2],["question",6],["issue",0],["solid",3],["trouble",2],["how",6],["subject",0]],"en":"What matters most in a small town is not how much you own but whether you can be counted on. That was my father's one subject, and he raised it at every table. The question of the new road came up again that autumn, and it was the least of anyone's concern at first. Then the issue of the solid ground under it turned out to be serious. There was real trouble at the meeting. My father said the matter was simple: either you build it well or you do not build it. For once, nobody in the room argued with him.","zh":"在一个小镇上，最要紧的不是你有多少产业，而是别人能不能指望你。这是我父亲唯独爱讲的题目，每回饭桌上都要提。那年秋天新修那条路的问题又摆上来了，起初谁也没把它当回事。后来路基下面土质是否结实这一条，成了大问题。会上真吵了起来。父亲说，这事很简单：要么好好修，要么别修。这一回，屋里没人跟他争。"},"meet":{"tw":[["fill",0],["answer",3],["experience",2],["hold",6],["fit",0],["club",3],["cope",2],["next",6],["play",0]],"en":"The school held a swimming meet in the last week of term, and everyone in the club had to fill in a form and answer two questions about their health. My sister, who had little experience of racing, was not sure she would fit in. She had to cope with a bad start and a lane that was too narrow, and the hall was loud. She came fourth, not last. The next morning she told me she would do it again. She did not play any other sport that year. I think that was the first time I saw her really want something.","zh":"学期最后一周，学校办了一场游泳比赛，俱乐部里每个人都得填一张表，回答两个关于健康的问题。我妹妹比赛的经验很少，不确定自己能不能跟得上。出发没起好，泳道又窄，她都得扛下来，馆里还吵。她拿了第四，不是最后。第二天早上她跟我说她还要再来一次。那年她再没玩别的项目。我想那是我头一回看见她真想要一样东西。"},"mention":{"tw":[["note",2],["raise",3],["notice",2],["question",6],["credit",0],["remember",3],["state",2],["answer",6],["observe",0]],"en":"At the meeting nobody wanted to mention the money. I had made a note of it in my book, and I raised the question just before we closed. The chairman did not answer at first. He looked at the window, as if he had noticed something in the street. Then he said, in a flat voice, that the state of the accounts was not what we had been told. He gave credit to the woman who had kept the books, and he asked us to remember her name. I observed that one man at the end of the table said nothing at all.","zh":"会上谁都不愿提到钱的事。我在本子上记了一笔，快散会的时候把这个问题提了出来。主席起初没有答话。他看着窗户，像是街上有什么引起了他的注意。然后他平平地说，账目的状况跟我们听到的不一样。他把这份功劳记在那个管账的女人名下，叫我们记住她的名字。我注意到，桌子那头有一个人一句话也没说。"},"mistake":{"tw":[["slip",3],["stumble",3],["identify",2],["wrong",6],["fault",0],["blot",3],["misconception",2],["excuse",6],["error",0]],"en":"The clerk made one small mistake in the ledger, a blot of ink on the wrong line, and it cost the office a week. He had meant to write a name and wrote another one instead. It was not his fault; the two names were almost the same, and anyone could stumble over them. The manager let him explain, because she did not want him to look for an excuse. He did not slip again that year. He said later that a misconception is harder to fix than an error, because nobody can identify it. I have thought about that ever since.","zh":"那个职员在账本上出了个小错，一滴墨落在了不该落的那一行，办公室为此搭进去一个星期。他本来要写一个名字，写成了另一个。这不能全怪他：两个名字几乎一样，谁都会绊一下。经理让他自己说明，因为不想让他去找借口。那一年他再没出过这种岔子。后来他说，错的理解比错本身更难改，因为谁也指不出来它在哪儿。这话我到现在还在想。"},"noise":{"tw":[["racket",0],["background",3],["cry",2],["loud",6],["resound",0],["boom",3],["sound",2],["alarm",6],["dissonance",0]],"en":"The noise in the street that afternoon was a great racket, and above the background of the traffic came a cry from near the bridge. Then a boom, and the whole window shook. The sound of it resounded off the buildings on both sides. We ran out, but nothing was there except a lorry with a broken drum. Somebody had set off the alarm in the shop next door by mistake. It was so loud that my ears rang for an hour. My father said that what we had heard was not music but dissonance, and that he preferred it to silence.","zh":"那天下午街上的响动是一片大嘈杂，车流的背景声之上，桥那头传来一声喊叫。接着一声闷响，整扇窗子都晃了。那声音在两边的楼之间回荡。我们跑出去，什么也没有，只有一辆鼓破了的卡车。隔壁铺子里的警报被人误碰响了。响得我耳朵嗡了一个钟头。父亲说，我们听见的不是音乐，是刺耳的不谐，他还说他宁愿这样，也不要安静。"},"offer":{"tw":[["pass",0],["special",3],["act",2],["purchase",6],["crack",0],["hook",3],["market",2],["deal",6],["propose",0]],"en":"In the market a woman offered me a special price on a piece of cloth. I passed her stall twice before I made the purchase, because I could not see a crack in the offer. There was a hook near the door with a coat on it, and she kept her money in a bag under that coat. She proposed a deal that sounded generous until I did the sum. I did not act at once. She laughed and said I was the first customer that week who had counted. Then she took a little off the price, and I bought it.","zh":"市场里有个女人向我报了一块布的特别价钱。我从她摊前走了两趟才买下来——我看不出这报价里有什么破绽。门边有个挂钩，上面挂着件外套，她的钱就放在那外套下面的袋子里。她提的那个交易听着挺大方，直到我心算了一下。我没有马上答应。她笑了，说我是那一周头一个会算账的客人。然后她让了一点价，我买下了。"},"order":{"tw":[["arrange",2],["call",3],["act",2],["disorder",1],["allow",6],["club",0],["hunt",3],["rule",2],["rate",0]],"en":"The club had one rule about the order of things, and it was written on the wall in the hall. No one was allowed to call out a number before the chairman had arranged the list. The rate of the fee went up that year, and there was some disorder at the meeting about it. The old men would hunt through the papers for the same page again and again. I was told to act as secretary and keep the record. Nobody ever thanked me. It was, I think, the most useful year of my life. I learned more from those papers than from any book.","zh":"俱乐部对于次序只有一条规矩，写在走廊的墙上。主席把名单排好之前，谁也不许报号。那一年的会费涨了，会上因此有点乱。那几个老人一遍遍地翻那些纸，找同一页。他们让我当秘书，负责记录。从来没人谢过我。我觉得，那是我这辈子最有用的一个年头。我从那些纸上学到的，比从任何一本书上都多。"},"pack":{"tw":[["camp",0],["bag",3],["arrange",2],["pick",6],["carry",0],["nest",3],["fill",2],["grab",6],["ring",0]],"en":"We had to pack for camp in one afternoon, and my mother would not let me carry the bag until it was properly arranged. I had to pick what I needed, fill the bottom with the heavy things, and grab a coat at the last minute. There was a bird's nest in the roof of the shed, and a ring of eggs lay in it, cold and blue. My father put a ring through the handle of my bag so I would not lose it. He said the first rule of the road is to travel light. I did not. My bag weighed more than I did.","zh":"我们得用一个下午收拾去露营的东西，母亲不肯让我拎包，非要我先理整齐。我得挑出要用的，把重的塞在底下，最后一刻再抓一件外套。棚子顶上有只鸟窝，里面一圈蛋，又冷又青。父亲在我包的提手上套了个环，免得我丢了。他说出门第一条规矩是轻装。我没做到。我的包比我还沉。"},"pain":{"tw":[["bother",0],["try",3],["upset",2],["pleasure",1],["stress",6],["hurt",0],["distress",3],["stomach",6],["trouble",0]],"en":"The pain in her stomach came back every evening, and it did not bother her as much as it bothered us. She would try to eat a little and then put the plate aside. It upset my father more than he would say, and the stress of those months showed in his face. She said the trouble was not the pain but the waiting. There was real distress in her voice on the bad nights. But she would still take some pleasure from a warm room and a quiet hour, and that was what hurt me most. I have never been able to forget it.","zh":"她胃里的疼每天晚上都回来，这疼烦我们比烦她自己还多。她会试着吃一点，然后把盘子推到一边。父亲心里比嘴上难受得多，那几个月压出来的痕迹都写在他脸上。她说，难受的不是疼，是等。夜里厉害的时候，她声音里真有痛苦。可她还能从一间暖屋子、一个安静的小时里得到一点慰藉——正是这一点最让我难受。这事我一直忘不掉。"},"paint":{"tw":[["key",0],["charge",3],["coat",2],["brush",6],["pigment",0],["prime",3],["cover",2],["plastic",6],["rouge",0]],"en":"The painter came with a key to the back door and a brush in each hand. He had to prime the wall first, then put on one coat of paint and let it dry. He said the pigment in the cheap kind goes grey within a year. He would not charge us for the plastic sheet he used to cover the floor. My aunt wanted a small tin of rouge for her face and he brought it with the paint. He worked slowly, whistling. When he had gone, the room looked as if it had been given a new set of walls.","zh":"油漆匠来了，手里拿的是后门的钥匙和两把刷子。他得先把墙打底，再刷一道漆，等它干。他说便宜的那种漆，颜料一年就发灰。他给我们盖地板用的那块塑料布不收钱。我姑妈想要一小盒擦脸的胭脂，他连漆一起带来了。他干得慢，还吹口哨。他走了以后，那间屋子像是换了一套新墙。"},"pick":{"tw":[["choice",0],["decision",3],["choose",2],["spot",6],["clean",0],["pleasure",3],["knock",2],["chance",6],["foot",0]],"en":"At the market I had to pick a place to stand, and the choice was harder than the decision to come at all. I could choose between the clean spot near the door, where the light was good, and the shade at the foot of the wall. It was a pleasure to be out so early. A man came and gave a light knock on the table, and I moved my basket. I had one chance at a good morning, and I took it. I sold nearly everything by noon. I have never had a better day at that stall.","zh":"到了市场上，我得挑个地方站，这个选择比决定来不来还难。我可以挑门边那块干净的地方，那儿光线好；也可以挑墙根下的阴凉。这么早出来是件快活事。有个男的过来，在桌上轻轻敲了两下，我把篮子挪开了。好早上就这一回机会，我抓住了。到中午差不多都卖光了。那个摊子，我再没有过更好的一天。"},"piece":{"tw":[["bit",0],["base",3],["eat",2],["simple",6],["man",0],["black",3],["join",2],["pick",0]],"en":"An old man sat on the base of the stone wall with a piece of bread in his hand, eating it slowly. He wore a black coat, and there was a bit of thread hanging from one sleeve. He would pick the crumbs off his knees and eat those too. It was a simple meal, and he was in no hurry. When he had finished, he joined his hands behind his head and looked at the sky. I wanted to ask him something. I did not know what. He looked as if he had all the time there was in the world.","zh":"一个老人坐在石墙的墙基上，手里拿着一块面包，慢慢地吃。他穿件黑外套，一只袖子上挂着一根线头。他会把膝盖上的碎屑捡起来吃掉。一顿很简单的饭，他一点也不急。吃完以后，他把两只手交叉垫在脑后，望着天。我想问他点什么，可又不知道该问什么。他那样子，像是世上的时间全归他。"},"plan":{"tw":[["programme",0],["hope",3],["idea",2],["propose",6],["design",0],["engineer",3],["think",2],["deal",6],["project",0]],"en":"The engineer came to the site with a plan he had drawn himself, and he hoped nobody would ask him where the idea came from. It was part of a larger project, a government programme for the valley. He had to design a small bridge, and he proposed to build it in one summer. I asked him to think about the winter water. We made a deal on the price and shook hands. He said no design survives the first flood, and then he laughed. He was right. The bridge is still standing, twelve years on, and it has never moved.","zh":"工程师带着他自己画的一份方案到了工地，他盼着没人问他这主意是从哪儿来的。这是一个更大工程的一部分，一项针对这条河谷的政府计划。他得设计一座小桥，他提出用一个夏天建成。我请他把冬天水大的情况想一想。我们谈定了价钱，握了手。他说，没有哪个设计能扛过第一场洪水，然后他笑了。他说得对。十二年过去，桥还立在那儿，一动没动。"},"plant":{"tw":[["establish",0],["bed",3],["stock",2],["factory",6],["institute",0],["fix",3],["communicate",2],["facility",6],["embed",0]],"en":"The plant on the edge of town was the largest factory of its kind in the region, and the institute in the next street had helped to establish it forty years before. My father worked the night shift at that facility, and he would fix the same machine every week. He kept a small bed of flowers outside the gate, and he would communicate with them, he said, more easily than with the men inside. There was a stock of old parts in the yard, going to rust. Someone had embedded a coin in the concrete step, and nobody knew why. He showed it to me once.","zh":"镇子边上的那家厂是这一带同类工厂里最大的，隔一条街的研究所四十年前帮着把它办了起来。父亲在那座厂里上夜班，每星期都要修同一台机器。他在大门外养了一小畦花，他说跟花说话比跟里面的人说话容易。院子里堆着一堆旧零件，正在生锈。有人在水泥台阶里嵌了一枚硬币，谁也不知道为什么。他带我看过一次。"},"pot":{"tw":[["deal",0],["flood",3],["stake",2],["bread",6],["kettle",3],["lot",0],["belly",2],["cake",6],["mess",0]],"en":"There was a pot of soup on the stove and a kettle beside it, and the whole kitchen smelled of bread and cake. My grandmother had a lot of rules about the order of cooking. She would deal with the flood of relatives at Christmas by cooking for two days. The stake in the garden, which held up the washing line, was the only thing she would not let anyone move. She had a great belly and a laugh to match it. When she died the kitchen was left in a mess, and none of us could find anything. I still have her pot.","zh":"炉子上有一锅汤，旁边一把水壶，整间厨房都是面包和蛋糕的味道。我奶奶对做菜的次序有很多规矩。圣诞节一大家子人涌来，她就连做两天饭来应付。园子里那根撑着晾衣绳的木桩，是唯一不许人动的东西。她肚子大，笑声也大。她走以后，厨房乱成一团，我们谁想找什么都找不着。她那只锅我还留着。"},"pound":{"tw":[["beat",0],["flap",3],["blow",2],["ounce",6],["hammer",0],["thrash",3],["hit",2],["barrel",6],["poke",0]],"en":"In the yard behind the garage a man was trying to pound out a dent in an old wing with a hammer. Every blow made the metal flap and ring. He would hit it, stop, look, and hit it again. A barrel of oil stood beside him, and he knew the weight of it to the ounce. He did not thrash about like a young man; he worked with small, exact strokes. Once he gave the panel a light poke with his finger and shook his head. I asked him if it could be saved. He said cars can always be beaten back into shape, if you have the time.","zh":"修车铺后面的院子里，一个人正拿锤子想把旧挡板上的一块凹痕敲平。每一下都让铁皮颤着响。他敲一下，停住，看看，再敲。旁边立着一桶油，那分量他不用称也知道到几盎司。他不像年轻人那样乱砸，下手又小又准。有一回他用手指轻轻戳了戳那块板，摇了摇头。我问他还能不能救。他说，只要有工夫，车总能敲回原来的形状。"},"power":{"tw":[["force",0],["control",3],["state",2],["system",6],["king",0],["degree",3],["provide",2],["pressure",6],["index",0]],"en":"The power station on the hill used to provide light for four villages. The system was old, and to a large degree it depended on one man who could control the whole thing from a small room. In winter the load was heavy, and the pressure in the pipes would rise until the needles went off the index. He would open a valve by main force and stand there, counting. The state never sent anybody to look at it. He used to say he was the king of that hill. When he retired, the lights went out twice in the first month.","zh":"山上那座电站过去给四个村子供电。这套系统老了，很大程度上全靠一个人——他在一间小屋里就能控住整台机器。冬天负载重，管子里的压力会一直往上涨，直到指针跑出表盘。他会使出大劲扳开一个阀门，然后站在那儿数数。上面从来没派人来看过。他常说自己是那座山上的国王。他退休以后，头一个月就停了两次电。"},"press":{"tw":[["fight",0],["newspaper",3],["advertise",2],["news",6],["push",0],["rush",3],["count",2],["interview",6],["contract",0]],"en":"The press office was one room above a newspaper shop, and on a busy night the whole floor would shake. There was always a fight over the last telephone. A young man would push through the crowd with a sheet of paper and shout the count for the front page. They had to advertise twice a week, or the paper lost money, and the news went to the printer in a rush at midnight. I once sat in on an interview with the owner and he said a contract was only paper. I still read that paper every morning. It closed in the end, like most things.","zh":"报社编辑部是报纸铺子楼上的一个房间，忙的晚上整层楼都在抖。总有人为最后一台电话吵起来。一个年轻人会举着一张纸挤过人群，大声报出上首页的条数。他们一周得登两次广告，不然报纸就赔钱，夜里新闻赶着送印刷厂。有一回我旁听老板接受采访，他说合同不过就是纸。直到现在我每天早上还看那份报。后来它还是关了，像大多数东西一样。"},"programme":{"tw":[["plan",0],["bill",3],["system",2],["launch",6],["broadcast",0],["patch",3],["schedule",2],["aim",6],["syllabus",0]],"en":"The college had a programme for older students, and my mother signed up for it in her fifties. The syllabus ran to forty pages, and the schedule gave her two evenings a week. Her aim was simple: she wanted to read the news without help. The system was not kind to people who worked all day, and a few of them left in the first month. There was a plan to launch a second course the next year, and they would broadcast it on the local radio. The bill for the books was small. She finished the course, and she patched up her old dictionary with tape.","zh":"学院有个面向年纪大的学生的课程，我母亲五十多岁报了名。教学大纲印了四十页，课程表给她排了一周两个晚上。她的目的很简单：她想不用人帮忙就能读报。这套办法对整天上班的人并不友好，头一个月就走了几个。第二年打算再开一门课，还要在当地电台播出。买书的账单不多。她把课上完了，还用了胶带把她那本旧词典补了补。"},"push":{"tw":[["advertise",2],["bill",3],["deal",2],["pull",1],["step",6],["drive",0],["nose",3],["move",6],["fight",2]],"en":"My father had to push the cart up the hill every morning, and he would never let anyone pull it for him. Step by step, with his nose almost touching the handle, he would move it two hundred metres to the market. The deal he had with the shop next door was that he took their boxes as well. He did not advertise; people simply knew. He would fight the wind and the wet road without a word. At the end of the month he would pay every bill on the same day. He said a man who drives himself does not need anyone to drive him.","zh":"每天早上父亲都得把车推上坡，他从不让别人替他拉。一步一步，鼻子几乎贴到车把上，他把车挪两百米推到市场。他跟隔壁铺子说好的事是：再帮他们捎上箱子。他不做广告，人们自己知道。风、湿滑的路，他一句话不说地对着干。到了月底，他同一天把每笔账都结清。他说，自己开车的人，用不着别人来开。"},"rate":{"tw":[["order",0],["beat",3],["charge",2],["increase",6],["grade",0],["seed",3],["measure",2],["rise",6],["range",0]],"en":"The rate they paid for the seed began to rise that spring, and it threw the whole order of the work out. My father had to measure every sack twice and then increase his price by a small amount. He would beat the old grade of wheat into the ground and try a new one. The range of what he could grow on that soil was narrow. Some years he made nothing at all, and the charge for the mill came out of his own pocket. He never missed a payment. He said a rate is not a promise, it is only weather written down.","zh":"那年春天种子的价钱涨了，把整个活计的次序都打乱了。父亲得把每袋量两遍，再把他的卖价往上提一点。他会把旧等级的小麦砸进地里，试一种新的。那块土上能种什么，范围很窄。有的年份他什么也没挣着，磨坊的钱还得从自己兜里出。他从没欠过一次账。他说，价钱不是承诺，只是把天气写下来而已。"},"reach":{"tw":[["hand",0],["deal",3],["arrive",2],["rest",6],["hit",0],["find",3],["move",2],["chance",6],["pass",0]],"en":"We had to reach the village before dark, and my father would not rest on the way. He would find the path by hand when it grew too black to see. The wind began to hit us from the left, and every chance of a shortcut was gone. He did not move quickly; he was past sixty, and he had made a quiet deal with the road. We passed two empty farms and a broken bridge. When we arrived, the inn was shut. He sat on the step and said that a man can get anywhere, if he does not mind being tired.","zh":"我们得在天黑前赶到那个村子，父亲一路上不肯歇。黑得看不清路的时候，他用手摸着找道。风开始从左边打过来，走近路的指望全没了。他走得不快，六十多了，跟这条路之间有一种不说出口的默契。我们经过两座空农舍和一座断桥。到的时候，客栈已经关了。他坐在台阶上说，一个人哪儿都到得了，只要不怕累。"},"read":{"tw":[["record",0],["call",3],["talk",2],["write",6],["say",3],["strike",3],["understand",2],["copy",6],["study",0]],"en":"My grandfather could not read until he was fourteen, and he never let anyone forget it. He would study a page for an hour and then say only that he did not understand it. In the evenings he would ask my mother to read the record of the farm aloud, and he would copy the figures into his own book. A word would strike him and he would stop everything. When the school called about me, he went himself and had a long talk with the head. He could not write his name, but he could tell a good teacher from a bad one.","zh":"我爷爷十四岁才会读书，这事他从不让人忘掉。一页纸他能看上整整一个钟头，然后只说一句他看不懂。傍晚他让我母亲把农场的账念出来，他把那些数字抄进自己的本子里。碰到一个让他心里一动的词，他会把手里的事全停下。学校为我打电话来的时候，他自己跑了一趟，跟校长谈了很久。他连自己的名字都写不了，可他能分得出好老师和坏老师。"},"red":{"tw":[["loss",0],["squeeze",3],["radical",2],["yellow",6],["scarlet",3],["cardinal",3],["sum",2],["blue",6],["crimson",3]],"en":"The fabric shop had one wall of red cloth, and the woman there could tell scarlet from crimson without looking twice. She said the yellow and the blue on the next shelf had been there a year, but the red moved. A radical change in fashion had come that spring, and nobody could explain the sum of it. Her loss that winter had been heavy, and she had to squeeze every coin. A cardinal once came into the shop, in his dark coat, and bought a metre of the plainest stuff. She told the story for years. Red was the only colour she trusted.","zh":"那家布店里有一面墙全是红布，店里的女人一眼就能分出猩红和深红。她说旁边架子上的黄的和蓝的搁了一年了，红的一直在动。那年春天风气变了个大的，谁也说不清加起来是怎么回事。她那年冬天亏得厉害，一个铜板都得抠着花。有一次一位红衣主教穿着深色外套进店，买了两尺最素的料子。这故事她讲了好多年。红色是她唯一信得过的颜色。"},"relate":{"tw":[["concern",0],["involve",3],["tell",2],["understand",6],["touch",0],["remember",3],["think",2],["describe",6],["associate",0]],"en":"My aunt would never tell a story straight. She would describe a room, a smell, the way a hand touched a shoulder, and only then come to what the thing was about. As a child I could not understand why she took so long. Now I think it was her way of saying that everything is related to everything else. She had a concern for small facts, and she would remember a date from forty years back. Anything that did not involve her she still talked about as if it did. I associate her voice with that kitchen. It smelled of apples and wet stone.","zh":"我姑妈从来不会直着讲故事。她先说一间屋子、一种气味、一只手搭上肩膀的样子，然后才说到事情本身。小时候我不明白她为什么要绕这么久。现在我想，她是在说，什么跟什么都是连着的。她对小事很在意，四十年前的一个日子她都记得。凡是跟她没干系的事，她讲起来也像跟自己有关。我一想起她的声音，就想到那间厨房。里面是苹果和湿石头的味道。"},"report":{"tw":[["cover",0],["exclusive",3],["inform",2],["according",6],["paper",0],["gossip",3],["news",2],["press",6],["story",0]],"en":"According to the report in the local paper, the fire had started in a shed. The press sent one man to cover it, and he got an exclusive from a neighbour who had seen everything. The story was full of gossip about the family, and half of it was not true. He had to inform the office by telephone from the pub, because there was no other line. My father read the paper twice that night and said nothing. Then he folded it and put it under the coal bucket. He did not like the news to be wrong. He said a wrong line is worse than no line.","zh":"照当地报纸那篇报道说的，火是从一个棚子里烧起来的。报馆派了一个人去采访，他从一个什么都看见了的邻居那儿拿到独家。那篇故事里全是这家人家的闲话，一半都不真。他得从酒馆打电话回报社，因为再没有别的线路。父亲那天晚上把报纸读了两遍，一句话没说。然后他把它折起来，塞到煤桶底下。他不喜欢新闻里出错。他说，一行错字比没有这行还糟。"},"return":{"tw":[["fall",3],["drive",3],["answer",2],["leave",6],["issue",0],["home",3],["bring",2],["end",6],["pass",0]],"en":"My uncle had to leave home at nineteen and did not return for eleven years. He would drive a lorry for a company that never answered his letters. The issue was money, and he did not like to talk about it. When he came back, the whole village had begun to fall apart, and the mill had closed. He had to pass the old house twice before he could bring himself to go in. At the end of that week he told my mother he would stay. He did not say for how long. It turned out to be the rest of his life.","zh":"我叔十九岁就得离家，一走十一年没回来。他给一家公司开卡车，那家公司从不回他的信。症结是钱，他不愿意谈。等他回来时，整个村子已经开始散了，磨坊也关了。他在老屋前来回走了两趟，才狠下心进去。那个星期末他跟我母亲说他要留下来，没说留多久。后来才知道，是留了一辈子。"},"ring":{"tw":[["call",0],["tire",3],["sound",2],["triangle",6],["pack",0],["nest",3],["touch",2],["gate",6],["telephone",0]],"en":"The ring of the telephone would sound three times before anyone in the house moved. My mother kept it on the shelf by the gate, next to an old tire that my father used as a flower bed. When the call came, she would touch the receiver and wait, as if she were listening for something behind the voice. A pack of dogs would start up in the yard. There was a small triangle hanging in the nest of the old tree, and the wind made it ring all night. That was the only sound she really liked. I have never heard anything like it since.","zh":"电话铃要响三下，屋里才有人动。母亲把它放在大门边的架子上，旁边是父亲当花坛用的一个旧轮胎。电话一来，她会摸摸话筒等着，像是在听声音背后的什么。院里一群狗会跟着叫起来。老树的洞里挂着一个小三角铁，风一吹整夜都响。那是她唯一真正喜欢的声音。这样的声音，我以后再没听过。"},"rock":{"tw":[["shake",0],["roll",3],["move",2],["band",6],["stone",0],["crystal",3],["material",2],["pop",6],["tilt",0]],"en":"My brother's band practised in the old stone barn at the end of the lane. The rock they played was loud enough to shake the roof, and the whole floor would move under us. They had a crystal glass on a shelf for luck, and it would tilt and roll whenever the drums started. The material on the walls was too thin for that kind of noise, but nobody minded. People from the village came and stood outside. Some of them hated pop and said so. I sat on a stone by the door and listened to all of it. That summer I learned every song.","zh":"我哥的乐队在巷子尽头的老石头谷仓里排练。他们弹的那种摇滚响得能把房顶震松，整个地面都在我们脚底下动。架上有一只水晶杯，当吉祥物用的，鼓一响它就歪过来滚过去。墙上的料子太薄，挡不住这种动静，可没人在乎。村里的人跑来站在外面听。有人讨厌流行歌，还亲口说了。我坐在门口的一块石头上，从头听到尾。那个夏天我把每首歌都听熟了。"},"roll":{"tw":[["wave",0],["ball",3],["bread",2],["hot",6],["wheel",0],["clue",3],["change",2],["cover",6],["wind",0]],"en":"Every morning the baker would roll out the dough and cut it into shapes, and the smell of hot bread would cover the whole street. He had lost a wheel on his cart the year before and never found the clue as to where it went. In summer the wind came off the water in long waves, and he would roll the cover of the stall down and wait. A boy would kick a ball against the shutters until he was sent away. Nothing about the shop changed for thirty years. Then one morning it did, and the street was quieter.","zh":"每天早上面包师都要把面团擀开，切成各种形状，热面包的香味会罩住整条街。他前一年丢了推车上的一只轮子，一直没弄清它到底去了哪儿。夏天风从水面上成排地吹过来，他就把摊子的遮布放下来等着。有个男孩总往卷帘门上踢球，直到被赶走。这家铺子三十年没什么变化。后来有一天早上变了，街上也静了些。"},"rule":{"tw":[["find",0],["order",3],["control",2],["regime",6],["govern",0],["dictate",3],["decide",2],["under",6],["normal",0]],"en":"The rule in our house was that nobody dictated anything at the table. My father had grown up under a regime of silence and had decided that his own children would not. He could not control much else in his life, so he governed that one hour. He would find a way to make everyone talk, even about nothing. It was not the normal way for a man of his time. He said that order in a family is not the same as peace. When he died we kept the rule for a year, and then we lost it. I still hear his voice at my own table.","zh":"我们家的规矩是：饭桌上谁都不许发号施令。父亲从小在一种沉默的管教下长大，他打定主意不让自己的孩子也这样。他一辈子别的事都管不了，就管这一个钟头。他总能想出办法让每个人都开口，哪怕是说些没用的。在他那个年代的男人里，这不是常态。他说，家里的次序跟安宁不是一回事。他走后这条规矩我们还守了一年，然后就丢了。如今在我自己的饭桌上，我还能听见他的声音。"},"sail":{"tw":[["sheet",0],["boat",2],["ship",6],["sweep",0],["run",3],["move",2],["fly",6],["cruise",3],["beat",3]],"en":"The sail of the small boat had been cut from a sheet that had once covered a bed, and it would beat against the mast in the wind. My father could not afford a ship, so he sailed that thing along the coast for years. He would run with the wind until the whole shore would sweep past us, and we would not move a muscle. On clear days we could watch the gulls fly out and a white cruise boat far off. He used to say that a man needs very little: water under him, air above him, and time. I have never owned a boat since.","zh":"小船的帆是用一条旧床单裁的，风里总是啪啪地拍着桅杆。父亲买不起大船，就驾着这个玩意儿沿着海岸跑了好些年。他顺着风跑，岸边一路掠过去，我们一动不动。天晴的时候能看见海鸥飞出去，远处还有一条白色的游轮。他常说，人要的东西很少：身下有水，头上有天，还有点工夫。那以后我再没拥有过一条船。"},"scare":{"tw":[["fright",0],["terrify",3],["fear",2],["mad",6],["panic",0],["awe",3],["stimulate",2],["blow",6],["dash",0]],"en":"A blow on the door in the middle of the night gave us all a fright. My mother would not show fear in front of us, but she went mad with worry, and I could see it. The whole village was in a panic for two days. It turned out to be a boy who had been paid to dash through the lanes and terrify the older people. My father did not shout at him. He said a scare of that kind can stimulate a whole town into something worse. Standing in front of the crowd, he had a strange kind of awe about him. Then everyone went home.","zh":"半夜门上挨了一下，把我们全吓了一跳。母亲在我们面前不肯露出害怕，可她心里急得快疯了，我看得出来。整整两天全村都慌了。后来才知道，是个男孩，有人给他钱，让他在巷子里乱窜吓唬老人。父亲没有冲他吼。他说，这样一场惊吓能把一个镇子激到更糟的地方去。他站在人群前面的时候，身上有一种说不出的威严。然后大家都回家了。"},"seat":{"tw":[["behind",0],["box",3],["space",2],["front",6],["bottom",0],["chair",3],["support",2],["rear",6],["sit",0]],"en":"I had a seat at the front, in a box near the window, and behind me sat an old woman who never stopped talking. There was no space between the chairs, and her knees were against my back. She had to support herself on the rear of the one in front to stand up. At the bottom of the hall a man was selling programmes. I did not sit down again after the break. I stood at the side and watched the crowd instead. It was easier than telling her to be quiet. I never went back to that hall.","zh":"我的座位在前排靠窗的一个包厢里，我后面坐着个老太太，一直说个不停。椅子之间没有空隙，她的膝盖顶着我的背。她起身得扶着前排椅子的后靠。大厅最下面有人在卖节目单。中场休息之后我没再坐回去，站在旁边看人群。这比叫她安静容易。那间大厅我再没去过。"},"secure":{"tw":[["fix",0],["hang",3],["close",2],["ensure",6],["good",0],["tie",3],["attach",2],["maintain",6],["insure",0]],"en":"We had to secure the boat before the weather turned. My father would tie the rope twice, attach it to the post, and then hang the oars up under the roof. He had to fix the loose board on the shed door as well. To ensure that nothing moved, he would pull on the rope with his whole weight and wait. He said it is not enough to close a door; you have to maintain the habit of checking it. The man who came to insure the boat once a year always said the same thing: a good knot is cheaper than a new one.","zh":"天要变之前，我们得把船系牢。父亲会把绳子打两遍结，拴到桩子上，再把桨挂到棚顶下面。棚门上一块松了的板他也得钉好。为了确保什么都不动，他会用全身的重量去拽绳子，然后等一等。他说，光把门关上说不够，得养成检查的习惯。每年来看船保险的那个人总说同一句话：一个好结比一条新船便宜。"},"send":{"tw":[["air",0],["blow",3],["move",2],["deliver",6],["charge",0],["express",3],["transfer",2],["help",6],["post",0]],"en":"My grandmother would send a parcel every month, and the post in that town was slow. She had to pay a charge for the express service once, and it arrived five days late anyway. She would move the box to the counter herself and wait while the clerk wrote out the form. She liked to deliver her things by hand when she could. In winter the air off the river had a hard blow in it, and she would stand outside with the box against her coat. She never asked anyone for help. You could transfer her to another town and she would find the counter.","zh":"我奶奶每个月都要寄一个包裹，那镇上的邮局慢得很。有一次她付了快递的加急费，结果还是晚了五天才到。她会自己把箱子挪到柜台前，等着职员填单子。能亲手送的时候，她喜欢自己送去。冬天河上来的空气里带着一股硬风，她就抱着箱子贴在外套上站在外头。她从没开口求过谁帮忙。把她换到另一个镇子，她也能找到那个柜台。"},"serve":{"tw":[["answer",0],["act",3],["move",2],["hold",6],["help",3],["admit",3],["spend",2],["rest",6],["service",0]],"en":"My father served in that shop for thirty-one years, and he would not admit that he had ever wanted another life. He had to hold two jobs in the first years and would spend his rest day behind the counter. He could act as cook, driver, or watchman, whichever was needed. When a customer asked something he could not answer, he would move to the back room and look it up. He did not serve people for the money; he said it was a service you did for the street. Nobody ever helped him close up. I did not understand that until I had a shop of my own.","zh":"父亲在那家铺子里干了三十一年，他从不承认自己想过换一种活法。头几年他得兼两份工，休息日也在柜台后面过。他什么都能顶上：厨子、司机、看夜的。有客人问到他答不上来的事，他就走到后屋去查。他服务人不是为了钱，他说这是给这条街做的一件事。从来没人帮他收过摊。这话我到自己开了铺子才懂。"},"service":{"tw":[["help",0],["none",3],["care",2],["private",6],["serve",0],["stand",3],["company",2],["travel",6],["overhaul",0]],"en":"The bus service in that valley had none of the comforts of a city line. The company ran three old buses, and they would serve the villages twice a day if the road was clear. A private car was a luxury nobody had. When the rain came there was no help at the stop, but my mother would stand there for an hour in it and still say a good word for the driver. The care they took with the old machines was real. Every autumn the company would overhaul each one, and then the winter travel was safe. She never once complained. The buses stopped running in the end.","zh":"那条谷里的公交服务，跟城里的线路一点没法比。公司只有三辆旧车，路通的时候一天往村里跑两趟。私家车是谁也买不起的奢侈品。下起雨来，站台上也没人帮她，可母亲还是会在雨里站上一个钟头，上车后还要替司机说句好话。他们对那些老机器是真上心。每年秋天公司会把每辆车大修一遍，这样冬天的出行才安全。她一次也没抱怨过。后来那几趟车还是停了。"},"settle":{"tw":[["decide",0],["clear",3],["accept",2],["aside",6],["fall",0],["judge",3],["agree",2],["dispute",6],["determine",0]],"en":"The dispute over the two fields had gone on since before I was born, and nobody could decide who was right. My father would set the whole thing aside each winter and say it would settle itself. Then the old judge came out of retirement and agreed to hear it. He spent a day walking the ground until the line between the fields was clear. He determined that the hedge had moved, not the stone. Both families had to accept it. The matter fell quiet after that, and the two of them spoke again. I think they were both relieved.","zh":"那两块地的事，从我没出生就争起，谁对谁错没人说得清。父亲每年冬天都把这事搁到一边，说它自己会了结。后来那位老法官退了休又出来，答应听这件事。他用了一天在地里走，直到两家的界线弄清楚了。他判定是篱笆动了，不是那块石头。两家都得认。这以后事情就沉了下去，两个人也重新说话了。我想他们都松了口气。"},"shake":{"tw":[["excite",0],["roll",3],["change",2],["pull",6],["rock",0],["fan",3],["drink",2],["hard",6],["shiver",0]],"en":"The whole house would shake when the lorry went past, and the plates on the shelf would roll towards the edge. My mother would pull the window shut and fan herself with a piece of card. The news that summer was enough to excite anyone, and the town seemed about to change. I would rock on the veranda and drink cold tea in the heat. It was hard to sleep. Once I saw my father shiver in July, which frightened me more than the news did. He said it was only the fever. He was never quite the same after it.","zh":"卡车开过的时候，整栋房子都晃，架上的盘子在往边沿滚。母亲会把窗关上，拿一张硬纸片扇风。那年夏天的消息，谁听了都激动，整个镇子像是要变。我就坐在廊下摇着，热天里喝凉茶。很难睡得着。有一回我看见父亲七月里发抖，这比那些消息还让我害怕。他说只是发烧。那以后他就不太一样了。"},"shape":{"tw":[["build",0],["chip",3],["body",2],["structure",6],["figure",3],["cup",3],["cause",2],["fit",6],["form",0]],"en":"The cup had a chip on one side, and that alone changed the shape of the whole thing. My father would hold it up and study the form of it, the curve of the handle, the way it fitted his hand. He said the structure of a good cup is a small piece of engineering. His own body was failing by then, and he had lost the figure he once had. He would build shelves in the shed to keep his hands busy. Nobody could tell him the cause of the chip. He liked the cup more for it. I keep it on my desk now.","zh":"那只杯子的边上崩了一小块，就这一块把整只杯子的样子都改了。父亲会把它举起来，看它的形，看柄的弯，看它握在手里的样子。他说一只好杯子的构造，就是一件小小的工程。那时他自己的身体在垮，原来的身架也没了。他在棚子里做架子，好让手闲不下来。谁也说不出那块崩口是怎么来的。因为这个，他反而更喜欢这只杯子。它现在放在我的桌上。"},"share":{"tw":[["deal",0],["cut",3],["use",2],["profit",6],["portion",0],["end",3],["attempt",2],["stock",6],["parcel",0]],"en":"The deal over the shop was that each of the three would take a share of the profit, and each would have a portion of the stock. My father's cut was the smallest, and at the end of the first year it came to nothing. He made one attempt to change it and was refused. He would parcel out the work himself and use his own van to move the goods. He never said a bitter word about it in front of the others. I only learned how bad it was years later, from a letter he never sent. I still have that letter.","zh":"关于那家铺子的约定是：三个人各分一份利润，各拿一部分存货。父亲那一份最小，第一年到头什么也没落下。他试过一次要改，被回绝了。他自己把活计分派下去，用自己的车拉货。在别人面前他从没说过一句怨话。过了好些年我才知道那有多糟，是从一封他从没寄出的信里看到的。那封信我还留着。"},"ship":{"tw":[["send",0],["forward",3],["board",2],["vessel",6],["transport",0],["tender",3],["move",2],["boat",6],["embark",0]],"en":"The ship was a small vessel that had been used to transport coal, and by that year it could hardly move. Men would send their boxes down to the harbour and then wait to board. A tender took them out in two trips, and the crossing itself lasted nine hours. Nobody embarked without a paper bag in hand. My mother would stand at the rail and look forward, past the bows, at nothing in particular. She said a boat is only a boat until the land goes away. Half the village came down to see it off. It never came back up the coast.","zh":"那条船是条运过煤的小船，到那年几乎开不动了。男人们把箱子送到港口，然后等着上船。一艘接驳船分两趟把人送上去，横渡本身要走九个钟头。谁上船手里都拎着个纸袋。母亲会站在栏杆边朝前看，越过船头，什么也不特别看。她说，船就是船，直到陆地消失。半村人都下来送它。它再没有沿着海岸回来过。"},"shoot":{"tw":[["charge",0],["break",3],["fire",2],["sneak",6],["film",0],["chip",3],["grow",2],["catch",6],["hit",2]],"en":"My uncle used to shoot with an old camera, not a gun, and he would sneak up on birds in the garden to get them close. He had to charge the battery for a day before each trip, and if the film was not loaded the whole morning was lost. He would catch a bird in the middle of a jump, wings up, and then grow quiet for an hour. Once a chip of stone hit the lens and he had to stop. He said a photograph is a small fire you keep alive. Nobody could break the habit. He did it until he was eighty-two.","zh":"我叔拍照，用的是台老相机，不是枪，他会悄悄靠近园子里的鸟，凑得很近。每次出门前电池都要充一天，胶卷要是没装好，一早上就白费了。他能拍到鸟腾空的一瞬，翅膀张着，然后他会安静一个钟头。有一次一块碎石打到镜头上，他只好停下。他说，一张照片就是一小簇你得看着不让它灭的火。这习惯谁也改不了。他一直拍到八十二岁。"},"shop":{"tw":[["store",0],["market",3],["course",2],["warehouse",6],["rat",0],["antique",3],["inform",2],["factory",6],["frequent",0]],"en":"The shop was a store of old things, and half of what was in it came from a warehouse on the other side of the market. My mother was such a frequent visitor that the owner would inform her of every new arrival. Over the years she took a course in antique glass, and she could tell a copy from the real thing across the room. There was a rat in the back that nobody could catch. In front of the door stood a table of small chairs made in a factory somewhere. I have the one she bought. It is the only thing of hers I kept.","zh":"那家铺子是个卖旧东西的店，里面一半的东西来自市场另一头的一个仓库。母亲去得太勤了，店主每有新货就跟她说。这些年她上过一门古董玻璃的课，隔着屋子就能看出哪件是仿的。后头有只老鼠，谁也抓不着。门前摆着一张桌子，上面是某个厂子做的小椅子。她买的那把在我这儿。她的东西我只留了这一件。"},"money":{"tw":[["monetary",4],["fund",3],["currency",2],["pay",6],["sterling",3],["wealth",2],["tax",6]],"en":"My parents saved money for years before they could buy the shop. They kept a small fund in a box, in notes of every currency they had ever earned. My mother said the monetary side was always the hardest part. She would pay the tax on time and count what was left. She did not care about wealth; she only wanted enough. Once she was paid in sterling by a traveller, and she kept that note for luck. Every month they put a little aside, even in hard weeks. The box was old and the clasp was loose. It is still in the box today.","zh":"我爸妈攒了很多年的钱，才买下那家店。他们在一个盒子里存着一小笔钱，是他们挣过的各种货币的纸币。我妈说，钱这一头的事从来最难。她按时交税，再数数还剩多少。她不在乎什么财富，只想要够用。有一回，一个过路人用英镑付了她钱，她就把那张钞票留着图个吉利。每个月就算再紧，他们也要存一点。盒子很旧，扣子也松了。到今天它还在那个盒子里。"},"mean":{"tw":[["base",0],["drive",3],["associate",2],["reason",6],["think",0],["mention",3],["change",6],["tight",0]],"en":"The old man who owned our building was mean in a quiet way. He would drive to the shop to save a coin, and he never once mentioned the broken step. His base was the money he kept under the floor, not any real plan. He could not think of a reason to spend, and no one could change his mind. He would associate with nobody, and he kept the door of his office tight shut. We thought him cruel at the time. Later I learned he had lost everything once, and never trusted the world again.","zh":"我们这栋楼的房东是个不动声色的吝啬人。为了省一枚硬币他会开车去商店，门口那级破台阶却一次都没提过。他的底子就是藏在地板下的那些钱，谈不上什么打算。他找不出花钱的理由，谁也改不了他的主意。他跟谁都不来往，办公室的门总是关得严严的。当时我们觉得他狠心。后来我才知道，他从前一无所有过，从此再不信这世道。"},"mess":{"tw":[["deal",0],["flood",3],["meal",2],["bad",6],["fix",0],["disorder",2],["stuff",6],["hole",0]],"en":"After the flood, the kitchen was a total mess. Water had come through a hole in the roof and turned the floor into a shallow lake. Boxes of stuff floated against the wall, and the disorder was hard to believe. We had to skip one meal that day. My father said there was a deal to be done with the insurance, and he would fix the roof himself. The smell was bad for a week. We worked in silence, carrying wet things out to the yard. My mother kept saying it could have been much worse. We had to throw away a whole shelf of food.","zh":"洪水过后，厨房一片狼藉。水从屋顶的窟窿里漏下来，把地板变成了浅浅的湖。一箱箱杂物漂到墙边，乱得叫人不敢信。那天我们少了一顿饭。我爸说保险那边有笔账可以谈，屋顶他自己修。那股味儿熏了一个星期。我们一声不响地干活，把湿东西一趟趟搬到院子里。我妈一直说，这已经算好的了。我们只好扔掉整整一架子吃的。"},"middle":{"tw":[["centre",0],["deep",3],["early",1],["east",6],["eye",0],["seat",3],["long",6],["heart",0]],"en":"I had a seat in the middle of the carriage, with a long view down the aisle. The train left early, before the sun was up, and headed east along the river. The water was deep and dark. I could keep one eye on the fields and one on my book. In the centre of the carriage a family ate breakfast from a paper bag. My heart was not in the journey; I was going to say goodbye to someone. Somewhere in the middle of the afternoon the light changed, and I closed the book and slept.","zh":"我的座位在车厢正中，一眼能望到过道那头。火车一大早就开了，天还没亮，顺着河往东走。河水又深又暗。我可以一只眼看田野，一只眼看书。车厢中央有一家人就着纸袋吃早饭。我的心不在旅途上，我是去跟一个人告别的。到了下午某个时候，光线变了，我合上书睡着了。"},"minute":{"tw":[["bit",0],["climax",3],["note",2],["kick",6],["hour",0],["pinpoint",3],["header",6],["moment",0]],"en":"The last minute of the match was the climax of the whole season. Our best player took a corner, and a tall boy met it with his head, a clean header into the goal. For a moment nobody moved. Then the whole stand gave a kick of sound, and even the coach wrote a note on his card. He had spent an hour pinpointing where the other team was weak. Every bit of it mattered now. The game had been dull until that one second. I do not remember the final score, only the way the ball hit the net.","zh":"比赛最后一分钟是整个赛季的高潮。我们最好的球员开出一个角球，一个高个子男孩用头顶上去，干净利落地把球顶进了球门。有那么一瞬，谁都没动。接着整片看台轰地炸开了，连教练都在小本上记了一笔。他花了一个钟头找出对方的软肋。此刻每一点都算数了。在那秒之前，这场比赛一直很闷。终场比分我记不清了，只记得球撞进网的那一刻。"},"oil":{"tw":[["crude",0],["grease",3],["cover",2],["gas",6],["petroleum",3],["bless",2],["supply",6],["anoint",0]],"en":"My father worked in a garage, where the smell of oil never left his hands. He would use thick grease on the wheels and check the supply of petroleum in the back room. Crude oil came in by lorry once a month, and he would cover the drums with a sheet. He also drove the gas truck when the other man was sick. On Sundays he served at the old church, where the priest would bless the water and anoint the sick with oil. He said the same oil had two lives, one for machines and one for people.","zh":"我爸在一家修车铺干活，那儿的油味从来没离开过他的双手。他会给轮子上厚厚的黄油，再查一遍里屋的石油存量。原油每个月用卡车运来一次，他会拿块布把油桶盖上。别人生病时，他还开那辆运送燃气的车。星期天他在老教堂帮忙，神父用油给病人祝福、涂抹。他说同一种油有两种性命，一种给机器，一种给人。"},"paper":{"tw":[["report",0],["tabloid",3],["cover",2],["print",6],["newspaper",3],["gazette",3],["press",2],["sheet",6]],"en":"The local paper came out once a week, and the whole office was three rooms and two old machines. The editor would print the news on a single wide sheet, and the press made a great noise as it worked. He wrote every report himself, from the school fair to the price of bread. He hated the big tabloid papers and would not cover a story the way they did. The old gazette had been in the family for fifty years. When people stopped buying the newspaper, he kept going for another year, then closed the door quietly.","zh":"这份本地报纸一周出一期，整个编辑部就是三个房间和两台旧机器。编辑把新闻印在一张整幅的大纸上，印刷机一开动就轰轰响。每一篇报道他都自己写，从学校的集市到面包的价钱。他讨厌那些大报小报，绝不按他们的路数去报道一件事。这份老报在他们家已经五十年了。等到人们不再买报纸，他又撑了一年，然后悄悄关上了门。"},"part":{"tw":[["break",3],["base",3],["change",2],["entire",6],["office",0],["bit",3],["concern",2],["piece",0]],"en":"The bicycle had one broken part, a small piece near the base of the frame, and it was the only thing wrong with it. I had to take the entire wheel off to reach it. In the office down the street they sold a new bit for three pounds, and I carried it home in my pocket. The change was easy, once I understood it. My only concern was the brake. I took a short break and then began. When I was finished, the old bike ran better than it had in years.","zh":"那辆自行车坏了一个零件，是车架底座附近的一小块，除此之外没别的毛病。为了够到它，我得把整个轮子卸下来。街那头的事务所里，一个新的小配件卖三镑，我揣在兜里带回了家。弄明白以后，换起来不难。我唯一不放心的是刹车。我歇了一小会儿就动手了。修完以后，这辆旧车跑得比好几年里任何时候都好。"},"pay":{"tw":[["bear",0],["charge",3],["settle",2],["cash",6],["salary",0],["foot",3],["money",6],["wage",0]],"en":"My first wage was small, but I was glad to have it. My father said I should settle every bill at once and never bear a debt. Once a month I would take my salary in cash and put half of it away. The shop on the corner would charge more than the market, so I walked further to save. Money was tight in those years, and we all knew it. When my sister needed new shoes, I paid for them without a word. It was not much, but it was mine, and I learned to keep one foot on the ground.","zh":"我拿的第一笔工钱不多，可我很高兴有它。我爸说，每笔账都要当下结清，永远别背着债。每个月我会把工资领成现金，一半存起来。街角那家店比集市上要价高，我就多走几步路去省。那些年钱紧，我们心里都清楚。妹妹需要新鞋的时候，我一声不吭就把钱付了。钱不多，可那是我自己的；我也学会了脚下踩稳。"},"perfect":{"tw":[["complete",5],["polish",3],["better",2],["good",6],["pure",0],["tense",2],["easy",6],["gross",0]],"en":"She wanted every note to be perfect, and she would practise until the room went dark. The piece was not complete yet; two bars still came out wrong, and she would polish them a hundred times. Her teacher said a good player must be easy with the bow, never tense. The tune was pure and simple, and that made it harder, not better. She would listen to the whole thing again, gross faults and small ones alike. On the night she played well, and nobody in the room moved. She was not perfect, but she was close.","zh":"她要求每一个音都完美，一直练到屋里全黑。这支曲子还没练成，有两小节总是出错，她会把那两小节磨上一百遍。老师说，好乐手拉弓要松，绝不能发紧。这调子又纯又简单，反倒更难，不见得好。她会把整首再听一遍，大毛病小毛病都不放过。演出那晚她拉得很好，满屋没有一个人动。她不算完美，可也差不远了。"},"photograph":{"tw":[["picture",0],["stereo",3],["record",2],["copy",6],["shoot",0],["photocopy",3],["nude",6],["snap",0]],"en":"In the old studio the photographer would shoot portraits all day, and on the wall hung a photograph of a stone statue, a nude figure in grey light. He kept a record of every job in a thick book and would make a copy for each customer. A picture of a wedding could take an hour; a single snap was quick. He had a photocopy of an old review beside the door. A stereo played quietly in the back room. He said the camera could not lie, but a person could. I went there once to have my portrait taken, and I still keep it.","zh":"在那间老影棚里，摄影师整天拍人像；墙上挂着一张照片，拍的是一尊石像，灰光里一个赤裸的身影。他把每一项活都记在一本厚册子里，再给每位客人留一份拷贝。一张婚礼照要拍一个钟头，随手一按的快照却很快。门边放着一份旧评论的复印件。里屋轻轻放着一台音响。他说相机不会撒谎，人却会。我去那儿拍过一次肖像，到现在还留着。"},"place":{"tw":[["home",0],["address",3],["move",2],["next",6],["lay",3],["end",3],["rest",6],["office",0]],"en":"This was the place where my grandmother died, in a small bed by the window. Her home had been there for sixty years, and she would not move, even at the end. I know the address by heart. In the next room stood her old desk, and on it she would lay her letters in a neat pile. The office where she once worked was far away now. When we sold the place, I took the desk and a photograph. Sometimes I put my hand on it and rest for a moment.","zh":"这就是我奶奶去世的地方，窗边的一张小床。她的家在那一住就是六十年，到最后一刻也不肯搬。那个地址我背得出来。隔壁房间放着她那张旧书桌，她总把信整整齐齐地摊在上面。她从前上班的办公室如今远得很。房子卖掉时，我要了那张桌子，还有一张照片。有时我会把手放上去，歇一会儿。"},"play":{"tw":[["act",2],["beat",3],["change",2],["game",6],["bet",2],["catch",3],["best",6],["bring",0]],"en":"Every Sunday the men would play a game of cricket on the field behind the pub. My uncle would act as captain, though he was the worst player there. He would bet a pound on his own team and then lose it. We would catch the ball badly and run in the wrong direction. The best player was a quiet young man who never said a word. When the light began to change, they would bring out the old scorebook. The team they could never beat was the one from the next village.","zh":"每个星期天，男人们都会在酒馆后面的场地上打一场板球。我叔会当队长，尽管他是打得最差的。他会往自己队上押一镑，然后输掉。我们接球接不好，跑也跑错方向。打得最好的是个安静的年轻人，一句话也不说。天色变了，他们就把旧记分本拿出来。有个村子来的队他们怎么也赢不了。"},"point":{"tw":[["charge",0],["address",3],["control",2],["close",6],["degree",0],["corner",3],["clear",6],["head",0]],"en":"At the meeting the young man made one clear point, and everyone stopped talking. The road bent at a blind corner, and a child had nearly been hurt there. He had the address of a man in charge of the whole district, and he would not let the matter close. The council said they could not control the traffic, but he asked for one small degree of action: a sign. He stood with his head down, reading his notes. Nobody could argue with him. Before the year was out, the sign was there, and the corner was safe.","zh":"会上，那个年轻人说清了一点，大家都停下了话头。那条路在一个看不清的拐角处拐弯，有个孩子差点在那儿出事。他拿到了全区分管人的地址，绝不肯让这件事就这么了结。镇上说交通管不了，可他只求小小一步：一块标志牌。他低着头站在那里念自己的稿子。谁也说不过他。不到年底，牌立起来了，那个拐角也安全了。"},"prepare":{"tw":[["cook",0],["dress",3],["change",2],["try",6],["fix",3],["lay",3],["bring",6],["ready",0]],"en":"My mother would prepare the whole meal herself and would let nobody help. She would cook for two days, dress the table with her best cloth, and lay a small flower by every plate. If something went wrong, she would change the plan without a word. She would try each dish before the guests came, and fix anything that was not right. We were told to be ready by seven. My father would bring out the good wine and open it early. Then the doorbell would ring, and she would smile as if nothing had cost her any effort.","zh":"我妈会一个人准备整桌饭，谁帮忙都不要。她要忙上两天，铺上最好的桌布，在每只盘子边摆一小朵花。要是出了岔子，她会一声不响地改主意。客人来之前，每道菜她都要先尝一口，不对的地方就调整。我们七点前必须准备好。我爸会把好酒拿出来，早早开了。接着门铃一响，她就像什么都没费过力气似的笑起来。"},"price":{"tw":[["cost",2],["rig",3],["worth",2],["market",6],["damage",0],["value",2],["drop",6],["toll",0]],"en":"In the market the price of fish would drop in the afternoon, when the ice began to melt. A good seller would never rig the scales, my father said, because a lie costs more than it earns. He knew the real worth of every box, and he knew the market better than anyone. The toll on the road had gone up, and that damage showed in what we paid. He would argue over a small cost for ten minutes. But when a poor woman came, he would give her the fish for half its value.","zh":"集市上，鱼的价钱到了下午就会跌，那会儿冰开始化了。我爸说，好卖家从不做手脚动秤，因为一句假话赔进去的比挣来的还多。他清楚每一箱鱼真正值多少，也比谁都懂行情。路上的过路费涨了，这笔损耗就落在我们付的钱里。为了一点点成本他能争上十分钟。可要是来了个穷妇人，他会按半价把鱼给她。"},"promise":{"tw":[["call",0],["bet",3],["guess",2],["pledge",6],["hope",0],["read",3],["bring",6],["anticipate",0]],"en":"He had made a promise to his daughter, and he meant to keep it. Every night he would call her from the road and read her a page of a book. He could not guess how long the work would last, but he would not break his word. He had made a pledge to her, and to himself. I bet he never missed a single night. He would bring her a small thing every time he came home, and it gave them both something to hope for. He learned to anticipate what she would like, and she was never disappointed.","zh":"他对女儿许下过一个诺言，也真心想守住它。每天晚上他都会在路上给她打电话，念一页书给她听。他猜不出这活儿还要干多久，但他不会食言。他对她，也对自己，立下了誓。我敢说他一个晚上都没落下过。每次回家他都会给她带点小东西，这也让两人都有了盼头。他慢慢学会了猜她喜欢什么，她从来没失望过。"},"put":{"tw":[["arrange",2],["load",3],["change",2],["back",6],["lay",3],["plant",3],["move",2],["order",0]],"en":"In spring my mother would put new plants along the wall and arrange the pots by height. She would load the wheelbarrow with soil and move it to the far end of the garden. Then she would lay each small plant in its hole and press the earth down. In the back of the house she grew herbs in an old box. She liked to change the order of the beds every year. She would stand at the gate and look at it, tired and pleased. By June the whole garden was full, and the neighbours stopped to look.","zh":"春天，我妈会沿墙种下新苗，再按高矮把花盆摆开。她装上满满一车土，推到园子最里头。然后她把每株小苗放进坑里，把土按实。屋后她用一只旧箱子种香草。她喜欢每年把几块花圃的顺序换一换。她会站在门口看着园子，又累又满足。到六月，整个园子都满了，邻居也会停下来看。"},"ready":{"tw":[["cook",0],["dress",3],["change",2],["want",6],["fix",3],["mount",3],["leave",6],["prepare",0]],"en":"On the morning of the journey nobody was ready. My father would cook eggs while my mother would dress the children and try to fix a broken zip. We had to change our plans at the last minute, because the car would not start. My brother did not want to leave his dog behind. He would mount the steps to the house and look back twice. We had spent a week preparing for the trip, and now we were late. In the end we left with the sun already high. It was the best holiday we ever had.","zh":"出门那天早上，谁也没准备好。我爸煎鸡蛋，我妈给孩子们穿衣服，还想修好一条坏拉链。最后一刻我们不得不改主意，因为车发动不起来。弟弟不愿把狗留下。他会走上屋前的台阶，回头看两回。这趟出行我们准备了一个星期，这会儿却要迟了。最后我们出发时，太阳已经老高了。那是我们过得最好的一次假期。"},"reply":{"tw":[["answer",3],["field",3],["state",2],["letter",6],["respond",0],["counter",3],["message",6],["response",0]],"en":"I sent a letter to the office and waited for a reply. A week passed, then two. I would check the counter by the door each morning for a message, but there was nothing. I did not know how to respond if the answer was no. In the end I wrote again, and set out the state of my case in plain words. Then a short response came, and it was yes. I read it standing in the field behind the house, with the wind in my face. I have kept that letter ever since.","zh":"我给那家事务所寄了一封信，等着回音。一个星期过去，又过了两个。每天早上我都会到门口的柜台看看有没有留言，可什么都没有。要是答复是不，我不知该怎么回应。最后我又写了一封，用最直白的话说明我的情况。回信很短，答案是同意。我站在屋后的田野里读它，风吹在脸上。那封信我一直留着。"},"rough":{"tw":[["approximate",0],["prepare",2],["smooth",1],["stretch",6],["fierce",0],["site",2],["pretty",6],["harsh",0]],"en":"They had to prepare the site before any work could begin, and the ground was rough. The plan was only approximate, so every day brought a change. A fierce wind came off the hill and made the men harsh with each other. They would stretch a long string across the field to mark the line, then smooth the earth with heavy machines. The site was pretty in the early light, though nobody said so. Halfway through the summer the work stopped for lack of money. Nobody came to finish it.","zh":"动工之前他们得先把场地准备好，而地面很粗糙。图样只是个大致的安排，所以天天都有变动。山那边刮来一阵猛风，吹得人人说话都硬邦邦的。他们会在地里拉一根长长的绳子标出线，再用重型机器把土碾平。清晨的光里，这片工地其实挺好看，只是没人说。到了夏天过半，工程因缺钱停了下来。再没人回来把它做完。"},"save":{"tw":[["write",0],["record",3],["spend",2],["help",6],["spare",0],["conserve",3],["chance",6],["preserve",0]],"en":"My uncle would write down every penny he spent, and he kept the record in a small black book. He did it not to save money but to remember. He would conserve the old house as it was, and never spend a pound on himself. A spare room was always ready for a visitor. When a young man came to help, he asked for nothing in return. He said the only chance we have is to preserve what is good. He was a careful man to the end. He would never throw anything away.","zh":"我叔会把花掉的每一分钱都记下来，账记在一本小黑册子里。他这么做不是为了省钱，是为了记住。他会把老屋原样保存下来，自己却不肯多花一镑。总有一间空房给来客预备着。有个年轻人来帮忙，他一分钱也不要。他说，我们唯一的机会就是把好东西保住。他一辈子都是个仔细的人。他什么也不肯扔。"},"say":{"tw":[["order",0],["add",3],["express",2],["why",6],["read",2],["answer",3],["want",6],["state",0]],"en":"The teacher would say the same thing every morning: read the question twice before you answer. She did not want a clever reply; she wanted the truth. She would order us to write one page, then add a second. When a boy could not express himself, she would sit beside him and wait. I used to ask her why the old books mattered, and she would state her reason without a single extra word. She was the best teacher I ever had. I have not forgotten that year. She taught me to be careful with words.","zh":"老师每天早上都说同样一句话：答题之前把题目读两遍。她要的不是机灵的回答，是实话。她会命令我们写一页，然后再加上一页。哪个男孩表达不出来，她就坐到他旁边等着。我常问她那些旧书为什么重要，她会把理由说得一字不多。她是我遇到过最好的老师。那一年我一直没忘。她教会我说话要小心。"},"see":{"tw":[["catch",3],["card",3],["bet",2],["why",6],["check",3],["care",2],["how",6],["consider",3]],"en":"From my seat by the window I could see the whole street. An old man sat at a table outside the cafe and played cards with two friends. I could not see how he won so often. He would check his hand, then bet a small coin and smile. I began to see why the others never left early. They did not care about the money; they cared about the game. I used to consider him the calmest man in the town. It was a small thing, but I would catch his eye and he would nod, and I came back to that window many times.","zh":"从窗边的座位上，我能看见整条街。一位老人坐在咖啡馆外的桌旁，跟两个朋友打牌。我看不出他怎么总赢。他会看看手里的牌，押上一枚小硬币，然后一笑。我渐渐看明白了，那两个人为什么从不早走。他们不在乎钱，在乎的是这局牌。我常常觉得他是全镇最沉得住气的人。这本来是件小事，可我好多次又回到那扇窗边。"},"short":{"tw":[["dead",0],["position",2],["long",1],["same",6],["light",0],["contact",2],["well",6],["little",0]],"en":"The visit was short, because the road was long and the light was already failing. We sat by the bed in the same position we had held for hours. My aunt was very ill, and the doctor said there was little hope. She could not speak well, but she held my hand. It was the last real contact we had. A dead calm lay over the house that afternoon. I have not forgotten that short hour. Nothing was ever said about it afterwards. It was the last time I saw her.","zh":"那次探望很短，因为路远，天光也快没了。我们坐在床边，保持着同一姿势好几个钟头。姑妈病得很重，医生说希望不大。她说不太出话，却一直攥着我的手。那是我们最后一次真正的接触。那天下午，屋里静得死沉。那短短的一个钟头，我一直没忘。后来谁也没再提过这件事。那是我最后一次见她。"},"mark":{"tw":[["check",0],["line",3],["add",2],["cross",0],["spot",3],["book",2],["note",0]],"en":"The teacher asked us to check our work and mark every mistake. She drew a line under the wrong word, then a small cross beside it. I had to add a note at the top of the page and write my name in the book. There was one spot of ink on the corner. I read the whole page again before I handed it in. That night I dreamed of red lines crossing the paper, one after another. In the morning I understood what she had been trying to show me.","zh":"老师让我们检查自己的作业，把每个错都标出来。她在错字下面画了一道线，又在旁边画了个小叉。我得在纸头上加一句批注，再把名字写在簿子上。角上有一个墨点。交上去之前，我把整页又读了一遍。那天夜里，我梦见红色的线一道道划过纸面。第二天早上，我明白了她想让我看到的东西。"},"market":{"tw":[["mart",0],["offer",3],["change",2],["stock",6],["bazaar",3],["class",2],["retail",6]],"en":"Every Saturday my mother went to the market and came back with a full bag. She liked the small mart better than the big shops, and she knew every stall in the bazaar. She would offer a low price, then wait for the change in the seller's face. The stock was different each week, and once she found a coat fit for a wedding. It was cheaper than retail, she said, and better made. She belonged to a class of shoppers who never paid the first price. I went with her once, and I could not keep up. She moved through the crowd like water through a gate.","zh":"每个星期六，我妈都去市场，回来时拎着满满一袋。比起大商店，她更喜欢那家小集市，市场里每个摊位她都认得。她先压个低价，再等卖主脸上的变化。货每周都不一样，有一次她找到一件适合婚礼穿的外套。她说比零售便宜，做工还更好。她属于那种从不照头价付钱的主顾。我跟她去过一回，根本跟不上。她在人堆里穿行，像水从闸门里流过去。"},"marry":{"tw":[["tie",0],["unite",2],["daughter",6],["wed",0],["officiate",2],["mother",6],["espouse",0]],"en":"My cousin decided to marry in the spring. An old friend would officiate, and the two families would unite for a single day. His mother cried when she heard, and his daughter carried the rings. The tie between the two houses went back many years. They chose to wed in a small hall, and to espouse their promises quietly, without a crowd. I was asked to hold the door. The hall was cold that morning, and someone had forgotten to bring flowers. It did not matter; nobody looked at the walls.","zh":"我表哥决定春天结婚。一位老朋友来主持，两家人会在这一天合成一家。他母亲听说后哭了，他女儿捧的戒指。两家的渊源能追溯好多年。他们决定在一间小礼堂里成婚，不声不响地互许承诺，不要人群。让我去把门。那天早上礼堂很冷，有人忘了带花。没关系，没人去看那几面墙。"},"near":{"tw":[["close",5],["push",3],["far",1],["outskirts",6],["dear",0],["where",6],["good",0]],"en":"The station was near enough to walk, on the outskirts of the town. My mother said it was close, but on a hot day it did not feel so. I would push the pram up the long hill, past the houses where the gardens were full of roses. She was dear to everyone on that road. Far behind us the factory smoke rose. That was the year I learned how good a short walk could be. Now the town has grown, and the station is no longer at the edge. But the hill is still there.","zh":"车站近得可以走过去，就在镇子边上。我妈说很近，可大热天里一点也不觉得近。我推着婴儿车上那道长坡，路过那些花园里开满玫瑰的人家。那条路上人人都喜欢她。远远的，在我们身后，工厂的烟升起来。就是那一年，我知道了短短一段路也能让人舒服。如今镇子大了，车站也不在边上了。可那道坡还在。"},"pair":{"tw":[["couple",3],["ride",3],["join",2],["behind",6],["match",0],["serve",3],["mate",0]],"en":"A pair of old shoes stood behind the door, a couple of sizes too small for me. I would ride my bike to the shop to have them mended, then join the queue and wait. The man behind the counter had a mate who did the work. He said the two shoes did not match, but that a good pair could still serve for years. I paid and left. They lasted two winters and one hard spring. When I finally threw them out, I stood by the bin for a while.","zh":"门后放着一双旧鞋，比我的脚小了两号。我骑车去店里修，然后排进队里等。柜台后面那个人有个搭档专门做这活。他说这两只鞋不是一对，可好鞋还能穿好多年。我付了钱就走。它们又撑过两个冬天和一个难熬的春天。最后我把它们扔掉时，在垃圾桶边站了一会儿。"},"park":{"tw":[["green",0],["lot",2],["hill",6],["common",0],["gear",2],["road",6],["commons",0]],"en":"On Sundays we walked through the park at the top of the hill. The green was full of children, and the road beyond it led down to the common. My father would leave the car in the lot and carry the gear himself. He said the commons belonged to everyone, and nobody should fence it in. We sat on the grass until the light went. Those afternoons are the clearest thing I have kept from my childhood. Nothing happened in them, and that was the point. My sister would run down the hill and back, and I would count the times she did it.","zh":"星期天我们穿过山顶上的公园。草地上满是孩子，旁边那条路通向下边的公地。我父亲把车停在停车场，自己扛着东西。他说公地是大家的，谁都不该把它圈起来。我们坐在草地上，直到天光暗下去。那些下午是我从童年里留下来的最清晰的画面。什么也没发生，而这正是它的意思。我妹妹会跑下山坡再跑回来，我就数她跑了几趟。"},"particular":{"tw":[["special",0],["highlight",3],["proposition",2],["general",1],["instance",6],["detail",0],["item",0]],"en":"There was one particular thing about that house I could not forget. For instance, the way the light fell on the stairs in the late afternoon. Every detail of it is still clear to me, though in general the rest has gone. My aunt would highlight a single item on her list each week and make it a small celebration. It was not a special day, only an ordinary one, but the proposition pleased her. I have tried to live that way myself, and it is harder than it sounds. You need patience, and a good memory for small things.","zh":"那所房子里有一件特别的事，我怎么也忘不掉。比如说，傍晚光落在楼梯上的样子。它的每个细节在我心里都还清楚，尽管大体上其余的都已模糊。我姑妈每星期会在单子上挑出一样，把它过成一个小小的节庆。那不是特别的日子，只是平常的一天，可这个主意让她高兴。我也试着那样过日子，做起来比听起来难。你得有耐心，还得记性好，记得住小事。"},"plus":{"tw":[["positive",5],["advantage",3],["quality",2],["minus",1],["extra",6],["resource",3],["regular",6]],"en":"The price plus the bag fee came to more than I had. On the plus side, the quality was high, and there was an extra discount for regular buyers. The seller said the coat needed little resource to make and would not wear quickly. That was a real advantage, my mother said. She counted the minus points too: no return, no change. Still, the good parts were positive enough. We took it home and it lasted for years. I wore it through two winters and one long illness. It never once let the wind through.","zh":"价钱加上袋子费，比我带的钱还多。往好里说，质量很高，常客还有额外的折扣。卖主说这外套做起来不费什么料，也不容易穿坏。我妈说，这是实打实的好处。她也没忘了算坏的方面：不能退，不能换。不过好处还是够多的。我们把它带回家，穿了好些年。我穿着它过了两个冬天和一场漫长的病。它一次也没让风透进来。"},"pop":{"tw":[["kill",0],["appear",2],["hop",6],["start",0],["drink",2],["music",6],["popular",0]],"en":"The little cafe played pop music all afternoon, and it was popular with the students. Now and then a man would appear at the door with a guitar, hop onto a stool, and start to play. Nobody tried to kill the noise; they only ordered another drink. I sat near the window with my notes. When the music stopped, the room seemed empty. I stayed until closing, longer than I meant to. The owner turned off the lights one by one and told me to come back soon. I did, for a while, every Thursday, always at the same table.","zh":"那家小咖啡馆一下午都放着流行音乐，学生们都爱来。时不时有个男人拎着吉他出现在门口，跳上一张凳子，弹起来。没人想把这声音压下去，只是又点一杯喝的。我拿着本子坐在窗边。音乐一停，屋里显得空落落的。我一直待到打烊，比打算的久。店主一盏盏关灯，叫我快些再来。有一阵子我真来了，每星期四，总坐同一张桌子。"},"problem":{"tw":[["job",0],["matter",3],["question",2],["change",6],["trouble",0],["puzzle",3],["possible",6]],"en":"The problem with the old pump was simple, but nobody had the time to fix it. It was my job to find out what was wrong. I asked one question after another and wrote the answers down. The change of parts was possible, though not cheap. The whole matter was a puzzle I could not solve alone. In the end we had no more trouble, and two men had it running by evening. They charged very little and refused the tea my mother offered. She said they were the last of a kind.","zh":"那台旧水泵的毛病并不复杂，可没人有空修。弄清哪里出问题是我的活。我一个接一个地问，把答案记下来。换零件是可行的，只是不便宜。整件事是个我一个人解不开的谜。最后我们再没出岔子，傍晚时两个男人把它弄转了。他们收钱很少，还推辞了我妈端来的茶。她说他们是最后一类这样的人了。"},"quarter":{"tw":[["draw",0],["kill",2],["drop",6],["tail",0],["divide",2],["net",6],["stern",0]],"en":"A quarter of the crew stood at the stern of the boat and watched the net come in. My uncle would draw it slowly, hand over hand, and divide the catch into small piles. A single bad fish could kill the mood on deck. He cut one into quarters and threw the tail to the gulls. A drop of water fell from his chin. The sea was flat and grey all around us. Nobody spoke for a long time. Then he laughed and said the fish had won again. We turned the boat toward the harbour, and the sun went down behind the hills.","zh":"四分之一的船员站在船尾，看着渔网收上来。我叔慢慢往上拉，一手接一手，把捕到的鱼分成好几小堆。一条坏鱼就能把甲板上的兴致全毁了。他把一条切成四块，把尾巴扔给海鸥。一滴水从他下巴落下来。四周的海又平又灰。好一会儿没人说话。后来他笑了，说鱼又赢了。我们把船转向港口，太阳落到山后面去了。"},"real":{"tw":[["actual",5],["coin",2],["nominal",1],["good",6],["really",0],["better",6],["material",0]],"en":"The coin in my hand was real, not a copy. Its actual value was small, only nominal, but it was old and made of good material. I really wanted to keep it, though my brother said a better one could be found in any shop. He did not understand why I held on to it. It was the only thing left from that house. For years it sat in a tin on the shelf, and I never spent it. Some things are worth less than they cost to lose. When I finally gave it away, the shop was closing and the man behind the counter was kind.","zh":"我手里那枚硬币是真的，不是仿的。它实际的面值很小，只是名义上的，可它很旧，用料也好。我真的很想留着，尽管我哥说随便哪家店都能找到更好的。他不懂我为什么攥着不放。那是那所房子里唯一留下的东西。它在那只铁盒里搁了好些年，我一次也没花掉。有些东西的价值，还比不上失去它的代价。最后我把它送出去时，那家店正要关门，柜台后的人很和气。"},"realise":{"tw":[["clear",0],["perceive",3],["know",2],["accomplish",6],["see",0],["fulfil",6],["understand",0]],"en":"Only later did I realise what he had meant. It was clear to me then that he had tried to fulfil a promise made long ago, and that he would not rest until it was done. I could see it in the way he worked. I did not fully understand it at the time, and I did not perceive how tired he was. Now I know. He had accomplished more than he ever said. I wish I had told him so. There is a lot I would say now, if the chance came back.","zh":"直到后来，我才明白他那句话的意思。那时我看清了，他是想兑现很久以前许下的一个诺言，事没办完他就不肯歇。我从他干活的样子里看得出来。当时我并没有完全懂，也没察觉他已经那么累。现在我知道了。他做成的比他嘴上说的多得多。我真希望当时告诉过他。如果机会能回来，我现在有许多话要说。"},"reason":{"tw":[["cause",0],["find",3],["present",2],["ground",0],["why",3],["think",2],["argue",0]],"en":"There was no reason for the delay, or none that anyone would present. I tried to find the cause myself, standing on the wet ground by the gate. My father thought it was the rain. My aunt would argue that it was the new manager. Nobody could say why the train had stopped, only that it had. I stopped asking questions and waited. In the end it came, an hour late, full of tired faces. I found a seat by the window and slept until my stop. Nobody ever explained it, and after a while nobody cared.","zh":"这趟误点没什么理由，或者说没人肯说出个理由。我自己站在门口湿漉漉的地上，想找出原因。我父亲觉得是下雨。我姑妈偏说是新来的经理。谁都说不清火车为什么停，只知道它停了。我不再问了，就等着。它终于来了，晚了一个钟头，挤满疲倦的脸。我在窗边找了个座位，一直睡到我的站。没人解释过，过一阵子也没人在意了。"},"sex":{"tw":[["gender",0],["tempt",3],["class",2],["abuse",6],["arouse",0],["distinguish",2],["homosexual",6]],"en":"At the clinic the clerk handed me a form with a line for sex. He said the word had been changed to gender on the newer forms. I was tempted to leave it blank, but he asked me to distinguish it from the line for age. A young man of another class sat beside me, and he said he was homosexual and did not mind the old wording. The question, he added, had begun to arouse a quiet debate. Nobody wanted any abuse of private details. I wrote my answer and handed the form back. It was the only honest thing on the page.","zh":"在诊所里，职员递给我一张表格，上面有一栏问性别。他说新表格里这个词已经改成了性别一项的另一种说法。我本想空着不填，可他请我把它和年龄那一栏区分开。旁边坐着一位来自另一个阶层的年轻人，他说自己是同性恋，并不介意旧的措辞。他还说，这个问题近来悄悄引起了一场讨论。谁都不愿意自己的私人信息被滥用。我写下答案，把表交了回去。那是那一页上唯一诚实的东西。"}}});
